window.YN_GUIDE = {"schemaVersion":4,"version":"2.2.4","pages":[{"locale":"zh","file":"index.html","title":"认识 YN","headings":[{"id":"主要功能","text":"主要功能","level":2},{"id":"使用要求","text":"使用要求","level":2},{"id":"下载与安装","text":"下载与安装","level":2},{"id":"配置","text":"配置","level":2},{"id":"按你的工作方式开始","text":"按你的工作方式开始","level":2},{"id":"yn-翻译项目例子","text":"YN 翻译项目例子","level":2},{"id":"质量检查","text":"质量检查","level":2},{"id":"2-2-4-更新摘要","text":"2.2.4 更新摘要","level":2},{"id":"文档与开发","text":"文档与开发","level":2},{"id":"隐私与许可","text":"隐私与许可","level":2}],"summary":"YN：开源 AI 小说翻译与游戏本地化工具 YN 是面向长篇小说与游戏文本的开源 AI 翻译与校对工具，支持全 AI、全人工和人与 AI 协作。 YN 支持 TXT、EPUB 和文字层 PDF，将 AI 翻译、AI 校对、原译文对照编辑与项目资料管理放在同一工作区。你可以把整部作品的翻译与校对交给 AI，也可以完全自己翻译，或只在需要的环节调用 AI。 长文本分块并发、译名与角色资料复用、格式自动保护和中断续跑，服务于跨章节、跨文件的持续翻译项目。 English · 下载 Windows 版本 · 使用手册 · 项目介绍 · 项目教程 · GitHub 仓库 适合需要跨章节保持译名、保护游戏控制符并持续推进长任务的文件翻译项目。PDF 使用横排文字层文档。AI 任务将所需文本发送给你选择的模型供应商。 主要功能 AI 翻译：按语言方向、文风和项目资料翻译整篇原文。准备阶段核对参数与内容，随后按行分块，由多个 Agent 并发翻译。程序校验行数、占位符和保留内容，独立 AI 复审覆盖全部机械风险行与抽样普通行，发现问题后自动返回精确修复。旧译可审计后选择性复用，长任务可停止和续跑。 AI 校对：对照原文检查已有译文的误译、漏译、术语、称谓和表达问题。逐片精审逐行检查；Monte Carlo 将全量程序扫描与分层抽样 AI 校对结合起来。结果包含具体行号、问题依据和完整替换建议，可自动应用到 HTML，也可逐条接受、拒绝或修改。 资料与一致性：AI 可整理译名与角色资料、提取新候选；翻译与校对复用正式译名、角色称谓与口吻、风格要求及已有译文。资料也可自行维护。 格式自动保留：翻译准备时，AI 结合任务要求与原文样例识别变量、标签和控制符等保留规则候选，程序试跑后在翻译与校对中执行校验；自定义规则可按需补充。 人工编辑与协作：在原译文对照页面直接翻译、逐行修改、搜索和管理项目资料；可从选中行向 AI 提问，或只把部分工作交给 AI。 PDF 提取与重排：提取正文及公式／图表资产，经机械结构整理、AI 修订与独立审计后生成 HTML；翻译后用译文和源资产重建结构化 HTML，自动重排导出 PDF。 详细参数、旧译复用、校对模式、局域网操作与产物位置见 功能手册。 使用要求 当前发行面向 Windows x64。安装包自带运行环境，普通使用不需要 Node.js。 使用 AI 功能前，需要在 YN 配置供应商、模型和授权；关闭 Agent 后仍可人工编辑。 原文应为 TXT、EPUB 或有文字层的 PDF。校对需要与原文逐行对应的已有译文。 下载与安装 在 Releases 下载安装版（Setup）或便携版（Portable）。本文介绍 2.2.4。 安装版支持应用内更新；便携版通过发布页下载替换。发布页同时提供 SHA256SUMS.txt。 配置 选择原文、项目保存位置、语言方向与翻译风格；使用 AI 相关功能时，在启动页顶部配置供应商和模型。AI 新任务默认每块 500 行、最多 3 个子 Agent；已有项目的显式设置会保留。 已有译名表、角色表或参考资料时，可先使用“整理项目资料”。有格式保留要求时，翻译准备会结合原文样例提出规则候选并试跑、校验；自定义正则和查看匹配示例可按需用于调整。 按你的工作方式开始 选择原文、项目位置、语言方向和风格；校对时绑定与原文逐行对应的已有译文。 选择 AI 翻译、AI 校对、人工编辑或混合方式。AI 翻译从“准备并启动翻译”开始；AI 校对需要已有译文。 需要人工参与时，可在对照 HTML 中逐行编辑、搜索、向 AI 提问，或逐条接受、拒绝和修改校对建议。 AI 处理或人工编辑完成后，点击写入最终 TXT 或导出 EPUB/PDF。校对建议的自动应用更新 HTML，最终文件通过写出入口保存。 完整教程 · PDF 说明 · 外部 Agent 后台使用 YN 翻译项目例子 日语 → 中文：Megido72（梅基多72）游戏文本翻译演示。 日语 → 中文：美希命的游戏汉化展示，包括其许多汉化游戏。 日语 → 中文：《命运石之门》圆环小说。 中文 → 英文：《Robotics;Notes》小说译文。 更多项目见 案例说明。 质量检查 YN 检查行对齐、占位符、保留内容、写入范围和恢复证据，并安排独立 AI 复审。发现的问题定位到具体行，可用于自动精确修复或人工处理。 质量检查 列出检查项目、测试来源和运行方法。 2.2.4 更新摘要 校对应用前自动载入完整译文并保留人工修改，避免 EPUB 等单文件导出出现空行。 翻译结束的可选警告审查提供“继续／跳过”选择，继续后自动续跑。 完整版本记录见 Changelog。 文档与开发 使用教程 · 功能与参数 · 工作流 · 技术术语 · 运行时代码地图 开发需要 Node.js >=22.19.0，使用已有 npm lock： npm ci npm run dev npm test npm run build 桌面、LAN 与发布包验证入口见 开发与验证。 隐私与许可 项目状态、资产、会话与备份保存在项目目录；供应商授权保存在 Electron 用户数据中。复制项目时，也需一并带走位于项目外的原文或资料并重新绑定。LAN 的 PIN 持有者可操作共享工作台，请只在可信网络或受控隧道中使用。 MIT · 第三方许可 感谢 OpenAI Codex 以及参与测试、翻译和反馈的人。"},{"locale":"en","file":"index.en.html","title":"Overview","headings":[{"id":"main-features","text":"Main features","level":2},{"id":"requirements","text":"Requirements","level":2},{"id":"download-and-installation","text":"Download and installation","level":2},{"id":"configuration","text":"Configuration","level":2},{"id":"choose-how-to-work","text":"Choose how to work","level":2},{"id":"projects-translated-with-yn","text":"Projects translated with YN","level":2},{"id":"quality-checks","text":"Quality checks","level":2},{"id":"2-2-4-highlights","text":"2.2.4 highlights","level":2},{"id":"documentation-and-development","text":"Documentation and development","level":2},{"id":"privacy-and-license","text":"Privacy and license","level":2}],"summary":"YN: Open-Source AI Novel Translator and Game Localization Tool YN is an open-source AI novel translator and game localization tool for long-form fiction and game text, with AI translation and AI proofreading. Choose a fully AI workflow, a fully manual workflow, or a mixed workflow with AI for the parts you choose. YN supports TXT, EPUB and text-layer PDF, with aligned editing and project references in one workspace. Chunked parallel processing, reusable terminology and character references, automatic format preservation and resumable tasks support sustained translation across chapters and files. 中文 · Windows downloads · User guide · Project introduction (Chinese) · Project tutorial · GitHub repository Use it for file translation that needs consistent terminology across chapters, preserved game control codes and resumable long tasks. PDFs need horizontal selectable text. AI tasks send the required text to your selected model provider. Main features AI translation: Translate complete source texts using the selected language direction, style and project references. Preparation checks settings and content, then parallel agents translate line-based chunks. The program validates line counts, placeholders and preserved content; independent AI review covers every mechanically risky row and sampled ordinary rows, with precise automatic repairs for failures. Existing translations can be audited and selectively reused, and long tasks can stop and resume. AI proofreading: Compare an existing translation with its source for mistranslations, omissions, terminology, forms of address and expression. Split review checks each row; Monte Carlo combines full programmatic scans with stratified AI sampling. Findings include row numbers, evidence and complete replacement suggestions, which can be applied to HTML automatically or accepted, rejected or edited individually. References and consistency: AI can organize glossary and character records and collect new candidates. Translation and proofreading reuse approved terms, character names and voice, style requirements and existing translations. References can also be maintained manually. Automatic format preservation: During preparation, AI uses task requirements and real source examples to identify preservation-rule candidates for variables, tags and control codes. The program trials the rules and validates them during translation and proofreading; custom rules can be added when needed. Manual editing and collaboration: Translate, edit rows, search and manage references in the aligned source/translation view. Ask AI about a selected row or assign only part of the work to AI. PDF extraction and reflow: Extract prose and formula/figure assets, organize the structure mechanically, then use AI revisions and independent auditing before generating HTML. Translated text and source assets rebuild structured HTML, which automatically reflows into an exported PDF. See the feature guide for settings, translation reuse, proofreading modes, LAN access and artifact locations. Requirements Current releases target Windows x64. Packaged desktop use does not require Node.js. AI features require a provider, model and authorization configured in YN. Manual editing is also available with the Agent closed. Use TXT, EPUB or a text-layer PDF. Proofreading requires an existing translation aligned with the source. Download and installation Download the installer (Setup) or portable build (Portable) from Releases. These docs describe 2.2.4. Installers support in-app updates; portable builds are replaced using the release page. Releases include SHA256SUMS.txt. Configuration Choose the source, project location, language direction and translation style. Configure a provider and model at the top of the start page when using AI features. New AI tasks default to 500 lines per chunk and up to 3 child agents; explicit settings in existing projects are retained. If the project already has a glossary, character bible or reference material, you can organize it before translation. When format preservation is needed, translation preparation uses source examples to propose rule candidates, then the program trials and validates them. Custom regex rules and match examples are optional tools for adjustments. Choose how to work Select the source, project location, language direction and style. For proofreading, bind an existing translation aligned with the source. Choose AI translation, AI proofreading, manual editing or a mixed workflow. Start AI translation from the start-page shortcut; proofreading requires an existing translation. When you want to participate manually, edit and search rows in the aligned HTML, ask AI about selected lines, or handle proofreading suggestions one by one. After AI processing or manual editing, use the controls to write the final TXT or export EPUB/PDF. Automatic proofreading application updates HTML; the write/export controls save the final file. Complete tutorial · PDF guide · Background Agent API Projects translated with YN Japanese to Chinese: Megido72 game-text translation demonstration. Japanese to Chinese: game localization demonstrations by 美希命, including many localized games. Japanese to Chinese: the Steins;Gate “圆环” novel. Chinese to English: a Robotics;Notes novel translation. See case notes for more projects. Quality checks YN checks line alignment, placeholders, preserved content, write scope and recovery evidence, then runs independent AI review. Findings identify specific rows and can support precise automatic repair or optional manual handling. Quality checks lists the checks, their test sources and reproduction commands. 2.2.4 highlights Load the complete translation before applying proofreading, preserving manual edits and preventing blank lines in EPUB and other single-file exports. Offer an explicit review/skip choice for optional translation warnings and continue automatically after review is selected. See the Changelog for full history. Documentation and development First run · Features · Workflows · Technical terms · Runtime map Development requires Node.js >=22.19.0 and the existing npm lock: npm ci npm run dev npm test npm run build See development and validation for desktop, LAN and release checks. Privacy and license Project state, assets, sessions and backups live in the project. Provider credentials live in Electron user data. When copying a project, also transfer and rebind external source/reference files. Anyone with the LAN PIN can operate the shared workbench; use trusted networks or controlled tunnels. MIT · Third-party notices Thanks to OpenAI Codex and everyone who tested, translated and reported issues."},{"locale":"zh","file":"guides.html","title":"第一次使用","headings":[{"id":"选择工作方式","text":"选择工作方式","level":2},{"id":"下载与模型","text":"下载与模型","level":2},{"id":"创建项目","text":"创建项目","level":2},{"id":"assets","text":"译名表与角色表","level":3},{"id":"translation","text":"启动翻译","level":2},{"id":"reuse","text":"使用已有译文","level":2},{"id":"proofread","text":"校对与写出","level":2},{"id":"pdf","text":"PDF、代码和公式","level":2},{"id":"中断与项目搬移","text":"中断与项目搬移","level":2},{"id":"lan","text":"手机与局域网","level":2},{"id":"让外部-agent-在后台使用","text":"让外部 Agent 在后台使用","level":2}],"summary":"第一次使用 YN English · 首页 · 完整参数 YN 面向长篇小说和游戏本地化，可选择全 AI 翻译与校对、全人工翻译与编辑，或人与 AI 混合处理。本页对应 2.2.0；先用一小段原文熟悉流程，再处理整本小说或整批游戏文本。 选择工作方式 AI 翻译：在启动页配置模型并使用“准备并启动翻译”。任务会核对参数和原文，再按行分块处理；可由多个 Agent 并发翻译，经过机械校验、独立复审和精确修复。 AI 校对：绑定与原文逐行对应的已有译文，选择逐片精审或 Monte Carlo 分层抽样。校对会返回具体问题与完整替换建议，可设置自动应用，也可逐条人工处理。 人工或混合编辑：生成原译文对照 HTML，直接修改译文；可选从选中行向 AI 提问、维护术语和角色资料，或只把部分任务交给 AI。 下载与模型 从 Releases 下载 Windows 安装版或便携版。使用 AI 相关功能时，在首页顶部配置供应商、模型和授权。AI 任务使用 YN 的配置；外部 Agent 发起任务也一样。 创建项目 选择原文和项目保存位置。TXT 支持单文件、文件夹与相邻行双语；EPUB 会提取工作文本；PDF 需有可选中文字。原输入保持只读。 语言方向和翻译风格是项目参数。默认每块 500 行、最多 3 个子 Agent；数量是并发上限，不是必须同时启动的工人数。 译名表与角色表 已有译名表、角色表或设定资料时，可让 AI 整理项目资料。这个入口可先创建项目，不要求已有译文；AI 整理并核查草稿后提交正式表，也可按需修改草稿。开始翻译后仍可在 HTML 中查看、编辑或删除条目。 启动翻译 简便准备会核对参数与实际内容。对你描述的保留要求，模型结合真实原文样例提出范围明确的规则候选；程序试跑规则并校验匹配，之后以 HTML 参数表中的同一组设置和翻译提示启动任务。翻译按行分块，可并发使用多个 Agent；每块经过机械校验，独立复审覆盖全部机械风险行和抽样普通行，失败行再由翻译 Agent 精确修复。已有译文可审计后选择性复用，停止的任务可续跑。你也可以先生成行对行 HTML，自行调整参数，再按需调用 AI。 保留规则按实际匹配位置保护内容，普通正文仍可翻译。自定义正则和查看匹配示例可用于按需调整规则，例如确认 abc: 只保护行首前缀而不锁住完整台词。用户明确要求不翻译的人名可记录为正式表中的“源词 → 原词”。 使用已有译文 绑定与原文行数对应的译文。旧译复用先机械快筛，再对风险行做语义审计；一次确认后保留可复用内容，只重译需要修复的行。译文与当前原文不匹配时，先解决绑定或行对齐问题。 校对与写出 校对需要与原文逐行对应的已有译文。逐片精审会语义检查负责范围内的每一行；Monte Carlo 将全量确定性扫描与分层抽样语义审查结合起来，抽样模式不会对每一行都做语义审查。校对结果定位具体行，包含问题依据和完整替换建议。 可选择将建议自动应用到 HTML，也可逐条接受、拒绝或编辑建议。AI 处理或人工编辑完成后，点击写入最终 TXT、批量写入或导出 EPUB/PDF。自动应用更新 HTML，最终文件通过写出入口保存。 PDF、代码和公式 选择文字层 PDF。YN 先提取正文、代码／公式字形和图表等资产，机械整理逻辑结构，经过当前模型的结构修订和独立审计后生成审阅 HTML。模型翻译可译正文，代码、公式及参考文献保留原始字形。导出用当前译文和源资产重建结构化 HTML，再自动重排生成新 PDF，无原正文文本框长度限制。已有 HTML 打开不重新跑结构模型。支持范围和资产限制见 PDF 说明。 中断与项目搬移 先使用停止按钮并等待收尾，再关闭或搬移项目。恢复在调用模型前核查草稿和证据；必需绑定文件丢失时恢复文件，不要让模型反复重试。项目内路径按项目根解码；项目外原文、PDF 或参考需一并拷贝并重新绑定。 手机与局域网 在桌面应用开启 LAN 同步并设置 PIN，手机或平板打开页面给出的地址。可编辑译文、审阅建议和使用同一 Agent 会话；桌面 YN 必须持续运行。公网隧道由外部工具提供，请保护 PIN 和访问地址。 让外部 Agent 在后台使用 给 Codex 等 Agent 阅读 官方 Agent API：先展示项目位置、模型和完整参数，得到用户确认后再准备并启动。接口是本地 stdio 协议与启动器，不是公开的网络服务；任务使用 YN 配置的模型，不使用外部 Agent 对话中的模型。"},{"locale":"en","file":"guides.en.html","title":"First run","headings":[{"id":"choose-how-to-work","text":"Choose how to work","level":2},{"id":"download-and-model","text":"Download and model","level":2},{"id":"create-the-project","text":"Create the project","level":2},{"id":"assets","text":"Glossary and characters","level":3},{"id":"translation","text":"Start translating","level":2},{"id":"reuse","text":"Existing translations","level":2},{"id":"proofread","text":"Proofread and write","level":2},{"id":"pdf","text":"PDF, code and formulas","level":2},{"id":"stop-and-move-projects","text":"Stop and move projects","level":2},{"id":"lan","text":"Phones and LAN","level":2},{"id":"external-agents-in-the-background","text":"External agents in the background","level":2}],"summary":"Your first YN project 中文 · Project · Full settings YN supports all-AI translation and proofreading, fully manual translation and editing, or a mix chosen for each project. This page describes 2.2.0. Try a small sample before a whole novel or game-text batch. Choose how to work AI translation: prepare settings and source text, then process line-based chunks with mechanical checks, independent review and precise repairs. Chunks can run across parallel agents. AI proofreading: bind an existing translation aligned with the source and choose split review or Monte Carlo stratified sampling. Findings provide specific issues and complete replacement suggestions, which can be applied automatically or handled individually. Manual or mixed editing: generate aligned source/translation HTML and edit translations yourself. You can optionally ask AI about selected lines, maintain terminology and character records, or send only part of the work to AI. Download and model Get the Windows installer or portable build from Releases. Configure the provider, model and authorization at the top of the start page when using AI features. External agents use this same YN configuration. Create the project Choose the source and project location. TXT supports files, folders and alternating bilingual lines. EPUB is extracted to working text; PDF requires selectable text. Original inputs remain read-only. Set the language direction and one project style. Defaults are 500 lines per chunk and up to 3 child agents. Worker counts are concurrency ceilings. Glossary and characters If the project already has a glossary, character records or notes, AI can organize them into project references. This workflow can create a project without an existing translation. AI prepares and checks drafts before committing formal assets; drafts can also be edited when needed. Tables can later be viewed, edited and deleted from HTML. Start translating The start-page translation shortcut checks settings against the actual source. For requested preservation, the model uses real text samples to propose scoped rule candidates; the program trials the rules and validates their matches before starting translation with the same settings and prompt used by the HTML controls. Translation is split by line and can use parallel agents. Each chunk gets mechanical checks, then independent review covers every mechanically risky row and samples ordinary rows. Failed rows return to the translation agent for precise repair. Existing translations can be audited and selectively reused, and stopped tasks can resume. You can also generate aligned HTML first, adjust settings yourself, and invoke AI selectively. Preservation rules protect only their actual matched positions; prose outside the matches remains translatable. Custom regex rules and match examples are optional adjustment tools. Explicitly untranslated names can be recorded as confirmed source-to-identical-target terms in the formal glossary. Existing translations Bind a translation aligned with the source. Reuse mechanically screens old rows, semantically audits risky ones, then asks for one batch decision. Accepted rows remain; only rows that need translation go back into the queue. Resolve binding or line-count mismatches first. Proofread and write Proofreading requires an existing translation aligned with the source. Split review semantically checks every assigned row. Monte Carlo combines full deterministic scans with stratified semantic sampling and does not semantically review every row. Findings identify the row, include supporting evidence and provide a complete replacement suggestion. Suggestions can be applied to HTML automatically or accepted, rejected or edited individually. After AI processing or manual editing, use the controls to write the final TXT, batch-write files or export EPUB/PDF. Automatic application updates HTML; the write/export controls save the final file. PDF, code and formulas Use text-layer PDFs. YN extracts prose, code/math glyphs and figures, organizes logical structure mechanically, then uses the current model for structure corrections and an independent audit before review HTML is generated. Translate editable prose while code, formulas and references retain source glyphs. Export reconstructs structured HTML from current translations and assets, then reflows it into a new PDF without original prose-box length limits. Opening existing HTML does not rerun structure models. See the PDF guide for supported inputs and asset limits. Stop and move projects Stop and wait for cleanup before closing or moving files. Resume verifies drafts and proof before model calls. Restore missing bound files rather than repeatedly asking the model to retry. Internal bindings resolve relative to the project root; transfer and rebind external sources, PDFs and references too. Phones and LAN Enable desktop LAN sharing, set a PIN and open the displayed address on the other device. Edit translations, review suggestions and use the same Agent session while desktop YN stays running. Public tunnels are external tools; protect the PIN and address. External agents in the background Give Codex or another agent the official Agent API guide. It must show location, model and full settings, wait for user confirmation, then prepare and start. The API is local stdio with a launcher, not a public network service. It uses YN's configured model, not the external agent's chat model."},{"locale":"zh","file":"features.html","title":"功能与参数","headings":[{"id":"1-项目-输入与文件绑定","text":"1. 项目、输入与文件绑定","level":2},{"id":"2-行对行翻译与审阅前端","text":"2. 行对行翻译与审阅前端","level":2},{"id":"3-术语-角色-文风与翻译记忆","text":"3. 术语、角色、文风与翻译记忆","level":2},{"id":"4-模型-provider-与-agent-会话","text":"4. 模型、Provider 与 Agent 会话","level":2},{"id":"5-ai-翻译-workflow","text":"5. AI 翻译 Workflow","level":2},{"id":"6-旧译审计与选择性复用","text":"6. 旧译审计与选择性复用","level":2},{"id":"7-ai-校对-workflow","text":"7. AI 校对 Workflow","level":2},{"id":"8-harness-host-与可靠性","text":"8. Harness、Host 与可靠性","level":2},{"id":"稳定性的设计依据","text":"稳定性的设计依据","level":3},{"id":"减少重复上下文的设计","text":"减少重复上下文的设计","level":3},{"id":"9-网页与本地参考资料","text":"9. 网页与本地参考资料","level":2},{"id":"10-局域网与远程操作","text":"10. 局域网与远程操作","level":2},{"id":"11-更新-恢复与兼容","text":"11. 更新、恢复与兼容","level":2},{"id":"12-pdf-与后台-agent-入口","text":"12. PDF 与后台 Agent 入口","level":2}],"summary":"功能与参数 YN 支持全 AI 翻译与校对、全人工翻译与编辑，或按项目混合使用。自动翻译、校对、资料整理和格式保留，与对照编辑、逐行提问及建议处理共用同一项目。 1. 项目、输入与文件绑定 新建、载入、保存和切换独立项目；项目设置、工作流状态、资产和会话都保存在项目自己的 .translation-workshop/ 中。 最近项目跟随实际打开或保存的项目，不会被文件选择器里的旧路径覆盖。 支持单个 TXT、文件夹、EPUB、文字层 PDF 和相邻行双语 TXT / EPUB。 EPUB 会提取成 UTF-8 工作文本；ruby 只保留基文，原始 EPUB 仍作为导出和重打包来源。 分离文件模式可分别绑定原文和译文；双语模式可指定奇偶位置分别作为原文与译文。 文件夹模式自动匹配源文与译文，并维护一个权威批次索引。 文件顺序支持阶段屏障。例如 A, {B, C}, D 会先完成 A，再并行处理 B/C，最后处理 D。 翻译输出和校对报告默认绑定当前项目的 AI_translation/ 与 report/，切换项目时不会沿用上一个项目的路径。 一个统一的分片大小同时用于初翻与校对；并发 Worker 数和独立复审 Worker 数分别设置为上限，实际数量会随任务量缩减。 翻译准备时，AI 根据任务要求和原文样例识别变量、事件码、标签与控制码等保留规则候选，程序试跑并校验匹配。也可按需添加自定义规则；无效正则会直接报错。 支持中英文界面、HTML 主题、项目级 Agent 代理开关和持久项目设置。 2. 行对行翻译与审阅前端 不启用 Agent 也能完成从读取、逐行编辑、搜索到写回的人工翻译流程。 单文件页和文件夹总览页；文件夹子页面、sidecar 与批次索引使用同一身份绑定。 原文与译文逐行对齐显示，支持直接编辑译文、保存人工编辑状态和刷新磁盘候选。 分页、页码跳转、全文搜索、滚动位置恢复、最近焦点行定位和文件标签切换。 按问题严重度标记行、显示高亮、清除问题、管理只读机械证据与可忽略项。 从选中行向 Agent 询问有界上下文，不需要把整份文件塞进对话。 校对建议包含完整替换文本；可逐条接受、拒绝或手动改写，也可按设置自动应用到 HTML。 一键应用已接受建议，并把批次内全部 canonical 子页面同步到当前译文。 AI 处理或人工编辑后，可写出最终 TXT、写回已绑定译文或导出 EPUB/PDF；写回前检查路径绑定、基线、sidecar、行数和冲突。 写回和覆盖前创建时间戳备份；原文文件始终只读。 旧版 HTML 打开时按明确版本标记自动升级到当前协议，不要求重新生成全部页面。 3. 术语、角色、文风与翻译记忆 正式术语表：项目内部的权威 canonical glossary。选择外部 glossary 后，工作流会同时保留 canonical 中不冲突的正式词；导入已接受候选时先合并现有 canonical、外部 glossary 与候选，冲突则整次拒绝，成功后再把项目绑定切到 canonical。 候选术语：Worker 只能在自己负责的证据行中上报新专名、译名和别名，不直接修改共享资产。 角色表：保存姓名、性别、代词、称呼、关系和口吻等可复用事实。 文风指南：保存作品级语气、表达偏好和格式约束。 翻译记忆：检索项目中已经接受的原译文对齐片段。 支持 JSON、Tab、=>、->、= 和逗号分隔术语输入。 行对行页面可编辑正式术语、查看和删除 AI 候选、逐条删除正式译名、搜索并替换译文中的命中项，以及导入保留的候选条目。 每个 assignment 只注入当前原文直接命中的完整结构化记录；缺失歧义才做单词精确搜索。 关闭候选收集只禁止新增候选，已有候选仍可作为只读参考。 正式译名优先，其次沿用候选或角色表已建立的译名；后来的不同译法只保留证据。尚无既有权威译名的新发现内部冲突才关闭新任务领取门，Parent 决策后再按当前清单生成精确修复。 glossary candidate、角色事实、DomainRun 状态和 Host 持久化在同一事务边界提交或回滚。 4. 模型、Provider 与 Agent 会话 支持 ChatGPT、Claude、Grok OAuth，以及 OpenAI-compatible API、API key 和显式模型目录。 Provider、OAuth profile、当前模型和默认 thinking level 是用户级配置，可跨项目使用。 Agent 网络代理默认关闭；只有当前项目明确启用时才会使用项目代理地址。 会话列表、创建与切换会话、独立弹出 Agent 窗口、流式输出和 Markdown 展示。 thinking、Function 调用和 subagent 以结构化对话 block 展示，不把内部协议文本混进普通回复。 支持图片输入时，根据当前模型目录声明决定是否开放附件。 显示输入、输出、缓存 token 和估算成本；支持 /compact、复制、Provider 设置、新建会话等产品内命令。 工作进行中可发送 Steer，当前工作结束后可排队 Follow-up；Stop 会终止活动 runtime 和 Worker pool。 Parent 与 Child 使用同一套 Pi Agent runtime、AgentMessage[] 和 Pi JSONL 会话。 长会话使用 Pi 原生 compaction；完整 Child 对话留在自己的 JSONL，Parent 只保存轻量状态和会话引用。 大会话按需读取；旧 v4 会话打开时自动压缩重复状态并保留可校验的 gzip 原文件备份，详见会话存储说明。 5. AI 翻译 Workflow 准备流程核对已设参数与真实原文；针对用户提出的保留要求，模型依据源文样例提出范围明确的规则候选，程序试跑并校验匹配。确认后沿用同一 HTML 参数表和正常翻译提示启动。 Parent 读取当前界面绑定和 Host 状态，选择不超过项目上限的实际并发数，并负责最终汇总。 Host 根据权威 manifest、文件阶段、统一分片大小、旧译复用掩码和现有证据规划真实债务；模型不能自创文件或行范围。 翻译池使用持久 Worker 动态领取互不重叠的 assignment，完成一块后再领下一块，避免每个文件私有队列造成长尾。 assignment 只获得自己的写权限；理解对话、代词或场景时可读取短邻近上下文，但不会扩大写入范围。 译文先写入 Host 管理的 staging，成功写入后立刻持久化路径、hash 和待审状态。 强制检查行数、空行、placeholder、标签、控制码、自定义保留规则和精确行身份。 独立只读复审池检查全部机械风险行和稳定抽样的普通行；普通行样本随分块大小增长。 复审只返回具体失败行与短修改要求，通过行不会逐行生成理由或报告。 失败回到写出该块的同一翻译 Worker 做有界精确修复，不重启整块翻译。 无进展或修复耗尽时，把 hash-current staging 和精确失败行交给 Parent 接管，保留其他有效行和既有证据。 术语冲突进入同一批次的 priority repair wave；修复清零前不会越过优先队列继续普通任务。 全部 assignment 结束后运行一次全文机械校验；如果仍有警告，YN 显示“是，继续审查／否，跳过”。选择继续后，自动完成剩余配对审查和必要修正；选择跳过则结束本轮翻译。 只有真阳性 warning 会成为精确修复债务；假阳性保存为 hash-bound evidence，避免重复花费 token。 Stop、崩溃或重启后可从持久 staging、ownership、evidence 和 Pi session 继续。 6. 旧译审计与选择性复用 默认关闭复用：完整初翻首次写入前对旧候选做 SHA-256 备份并清空一次，保证干净重翻。 开启后先对全部对齐行做机械快筛；行数、空行、placeholder、标签和明显占位文本错误直接进入重译。 非目标语言、原文复制、异常长度、重复译文、AI 污染和术语/角色/文风命中只是风险证据，不会自动判死刑。 无风险的目标语言对齐行自动复用；只有高风险稀疏行进入只读语义审计。 审计只返回 reuse 或 retranslate，成功提交后不再调用模型复述计数。 用户对整批只做一次选择；Host 事务性保留可复用行并清空重译行。 后续翻译队列只包含真实重译债务，不会为了连续覆盖把保留行再次交给模型。 冷启动按 owner、document、source hash 和保留基线恢复，不会把本轮刚写出的候选误当成启动前旧译。 7. AI 校对 Workflow 任何语义 Worker 启动前，Host 对清单内所有文档和全部对齐行运行 H3/H4/H7/H8/H9 等确定性扫描。 扫描结果绑定 source、candidate、glossary、character bible 和 style hash；输入变化会使旧证据失效。 确定性信号只是供 Worker 结合原文、译文和邻近上下文判断的证据，不会直接变成 finding。 逐片精审：Worker 语义检查自己范围内的每一行；分片大小只决定派发和保存边界。 Monte Carlo：Host 规划不重复的 HOT / WARM / COLD 分层样本，并记录真实覆盖。 Monte Carlo 将全量确定性扫描与抽样语义审查分开；抽样模式不对每一行都做语义审查。 达到最低轮数后，只有连续两轮无新增才算收敛；轮数上限仍有新增时由用户选择继续三轮、只精审 HOT 区域或按当前结果停止。 校对 Worker 只读原文、译文和项目资产，只能提交带证据的结构化 findings 与专名候选。 文件夹模式先预扫描全部文件，再把所有文档放进同一个跨文件 staged assignment 队列。 findings 按 scope 原子替换和去重，必须包含全局行号、问题类型、证据和完整可替换建议。 校对提示词携带项目保留规则，控制符、标签和占位符本身不作为正文错误；建议译文提交时复用翻译的结构校验，拒绝符号丢失、改动、数量变化和实际换行。 无变化修正、越界行、普通目标语言标点差异和格式不合格的提交会被拒绝。 单文件和文件夹都只持久化一份 findings JSON；人类审阅 HTML 由产品从该 JSON 生成。 8. Harness、Host 与可靠性 Runtime 负责模型调用、Function call、继续执行、Steer / Follow-up 队列、provider retry 和 compaction。 Harness 把 runtime、系统提示、Function 集、持久状态和完成条件组装成可持续执行的 Agent 环境。 Host 负责 manifest、assignment、阶段、写入 ownership、文件锁、hash、validator、事务与 completion gate。 通用调查、局部修复、完整初翻和完整校对分别拥有不同 typed operation scope。 完整批次在创建 Worker 前原子预留；重复活动批次会在模型 runtime 创建前被拒绝。 Parent 和 Child 可以按需读取参考，但只有 Host 授予的 document / range / exact lines 能写产物。 staging 提升、domain revision、alignment evidence 与 Host JSONL 持久化是一个可回滚提交边界。 可纠正的 Function 输入错误留在同一个 Pi turn；不可重试的内部或持久化错误立即停止整个工作流，保留产物和审阅证据并明确报错。 完成不是模型说“完成了”，而是 Host 确认所有任务、修复债务、证据、产物和最终校验都结清。 关键阶段、Worker、assignment、provider 错误、staging 与 hash 都有持久记录，便于停止、恢复和排查。 稳定性的设计依据 模型只做语义工作，文件身份、范围、并发写入和完成判断由确定性 Host 管理。 候选先进入 staging，不会把半成品直接覆盖到 canonical artifact。 翻译 Worker 与独立复审 Worker 分离，失败精确回到原 Worker；无进展会停止盲重试。 所有恢复依据都绑定当前文件内容 hash；过期授权和过期证据不能继续生效。 关键共享资产更新和产物提升使用事务，失败时尝试回滚；补偿无法确认时保留草稿、备份和诊断并停止。 减少重复上下文的设计 Host 自己规划分片和风险扫描，不让模型全文重读后再决定做什么。 assignment 只注入直接命中的术语、角色和短邻近上下文；缺什么再精确搜索什么。 机械快筛、placeholder 检查、行数检查和确定性校对信号不占模型推理。 独立复审只返回失败行，通过行不生成逐行解释。 Parent 不嵌入 Child 全对话，只读取轻量状态和结构化 discoveries。 旧译复用只把高风险稀疏行送入语义审计，保留行不会重新翻译。 hash-bound 通过证据和 warning 假阳性证据可复用，修改一行不会让整份文件全部重审。 9. 网页与本地参考资料 Agent 可读取用户明确提供的 HTTP(S) 页面并缓存可读正文。 Wikipedia 通过 MediaWiki API 提取正文；普通网页提取主要可读内容。 缓存参考可供 Parent 与 Child 复用，不需要每个 assignment 重新下载。 可只读访问用户明确提供的项目外绝对路径、旧译文和备份译文。 所有产物写入仍受项目边界、文档身份和行 ownership 约束。 10. 局域网与远程操作 在桌面应用中打开工作 HTML 后启动 LAN 同步，并设置 6 位 PIN。 手机、平板或另一台电脑可打开文件夹总览和单文件页。 远程端可搜索、翻页、编辑译文、接受或拒绝建议、同步页面并使用 Agent 面板。 远程 Prompt、Steer 和 Follow-up 使用桌面端同一持久 Pi session，不会另建一份远程 transcript。 SSE 只负责低延迟增量显示；断线或代理缓冲后，浏览器会从 canonical Pi messages 收敛到最终状态。 桌面应用必须保持运行；LAN 只共享当前工作会话，不开放任意目录浏览。 产品不内置公网隧道。需要外网访问时，可把 Cloudflare Tunnel、ngrok 等工具指向页面显示的本地地址。 公网地址等于暴露工作台入口。请使用不可猜测的 PIN，不要公开 URL，结束后关闭隧道和 LAN 同步。 11. 更新、恢复与兼容 安装版支持 GitHub Release 更新检查、下载和重启安装；便携版跳转到 Release 下载。 旧行对行 HTML、旧 proposal HTML 和旧项目字段有明确的升级与迁移路径。 旧分片设置只在迁移时读取一次，之后统一写入当前 canonical 设置。 Stop 会终止活动 runtime，但保留 hash-current staging、校对证据和未完成债务。 显式继续会在同一个 Pi session 与 Host batch 中恢复，不另起一批假装重跑。 Provider 传输错误保留脱敏 cause、provider、model、session 和重试记录，便于定位真实失败。 12. PDF 与后台 Agent 入口 横排文字层 PDF 会先提取正文、原生字形和图表资产，机械整理逻辑结构，再由当前 Pi 模型修订剩余结构问题并进行独立审计，通过后生成审阅 HTML。翻译可译正文后，程序使用当前译文和保留资产重建结构化 HTML，并自动重排生成 PDF；原文保持只读。已有 HTML 打开时恢复已保存译文，不重新运行结构模型。详见 PDF 说明。 外部 Agent 使用 官方 Agent API 先预览位置、模型和参数，确认后复用首页同一准备与启动链路。它使用 YN 配置的供应商，不借用外部 Agent 当前聊天的模型。 English · 首次使用 · 首页"},{"locale":"en","file":"features.en.html","title":"Features and settings","headings":[{"id":"1-projects-inputs-and-bindings","text":"1. Projects, inputs, and bindings","level":2},{"id":"2-line-by-line-translation-and-review-frontend","text":"2. Line-by-line translation and review frontend","level":2},{"id":"3-terminology-characters-style-and-memory","text":"3. Terminology, characters, style, and memory","level":2},{"id":"4-models-providers-and-agent-sessions","text":"4. Models, Providers, and Agent sessions","level":2},{"id":"5-ai-translation-workflow","text":"5. AI translation Workflow","level":2},{"id":"6-existing-translation-audit-and-selective-reuse","text":"6. Existing-translation audit and selective reuse","level":2},{"id":"7-ai-proofreading-workflow","text":"7. AI proofreading Workflow","level":2},{"id":"8-harness-host-and-reliability","text":"8. Harness, Host, and reliability","level":2},{"id":"reliability-mechanisms","text":"Reliability mechanisms","level":3},{"id":"reducing-repeated-context","text":"Reducing repeated context","level":3},{"id":"9-web-and-local-references","text":"9. Web and local references","level":2},{"id":"10-lan-and-remote-operation","text":"10. LAN and remote operation","level":2},{"id":"11-updates-recovery-and-compatibility","text":"11. Updates, recovery, and compatibility","level":2},{"id":"12-pdf-and-background-agent-access","text":"12. PDF and background Agent access","level":2}],"summary":"Features and settings YN supports all-AI translation and proofreading, fully manual translation and editing, or a mix chosen for each project. Automatic translation, proofreading, reference preparation and format preservation share the same project with aligned editing, selected-row questions and suggestion handling. 1. Projects, inputs, and bindings Create, load, save, and switch isolated projects. Settings, workflow state, assets, and sessions live under each project's .translation-workshop/ directory. The recent-project pointer follows the project actually opened or saved. Supports TXT files, folders, EPUB, text-layer PDF, and adjacent-line bilingual TXT / EPUB. EPUB becomes UTF-8 working text; ruby extraction keeps base text only, while the original EPUB remains export and repack metadata. Separate-file mode binds source and translation independently. Bilingual mode assigns the first or second adjacent position to each language. Folder mode matches source and translation documents and maintains one authoritative batch index. Ordered folder stages support barriers. A, {B, C}, D completes A, runs B/C in parallel, then starts D. Translation and report outputs rebind to the current project's AI_translation/ and report/ directories when projects change. One canonical chunk size drives translation and proofreading. Translation and review Worker counts are ceilings that shrink to actual demand. During preparation, AI uses task requirements and source examples to identify preservation-rule candidates for variables, event codes, tags and control codes. The program trials the rules and validates their matches. Custom rules can also be added when needed; invalid regular expressions fail visibly. Chinese/English UI, HTML themes, a project Agent-proxy switch, and persistent project settings. 2. Line-by-line translation and review frontend A complete manual workflow from reading and row editing through search and safe write-back, with no Agent required. Single-file pages and folder indexes with one canonical child HTML / sidecar identity per batch document. Aligned source and translation rows, direct candidate editing, human-edit state, and disk refresh. Pagination, page jump, full-text search, scroll restoration, last-focused-row location, and file tabs. Issue severity, row highlighting, explicit clearing, read-only mechanical evidence, and ignore handling. Ask the Agent about bounded context from a selected row without loading the whole document into chat. Proofreading suggestions contain complete replacement text. Accept, reject or edit them individually, or configure automatic application to HTML. Apply accepted proposals in one action and synchronize every canonical child in a folder batch. After AI processing or manual editing, write the final TXT, update the bound translation or export EPUB/PDF. Writing checks bindings, baselines, sidecars, line counts and conflicts. Timestamped backups before overwrite. Source files are always read-only. Legacy HTML upgrades through explicit protocol markers when opened; users do not need to regenerate every page. 3. Terminology, characters, style, and memory Approved glossary: the project's canonical glossary. A selected external glossary remains authoritative for overlapping terms while nonconflicting canonical entries stay available. Importing accepted candidates consolidates the existing canonical glossary, the external glossary, and the candidates; conflicts reject the whole operation, and only a successful merge switches the project binding to canonical. Glossary candidates: evidence-backed names, targets, and aliases discovered only inside a Worker's owned rows. Character bible: reusable names, gender, pronouns, forms of address, relationships, and voice facts. Style guide: title-level tone, expression, and formatting constraints. Translation memory: search across accepted source/translation segments. Glossary input supports JSON, Tab, =>, ->, =, and comma-separated records. The line-review page can edit and delete approved terms, preview/search/delete AI candidates before import, and search and replace translation matches. Each assignment receives only directly matched full structured records. Missing ambiguity uses exact-term search. Disabling candidate collection blocks new discoveries but keeps existing candidates readable. Approved targets take priority, followed by the first established candidate/character target; later differing observations remain evidence. Only internally conflicting new discoveries without an established target close the claim gate for Parent resolution and precise repair. Candidate assets, character facts, DomainRun state, and Host persistence commit or roll back together. 4. Models, Providers, and Agent sessions ChatGPT, Claude, and Grok OAuth, plus OpenAI-compatible APIs, API keys, and explicit model catalogs. Provider, OAuth profile, selected model, and default thinking level are user-level settings shared across projects. Agent proxying is off by default and is used only when explicitly enabled for the current project. Session list, session creation and switching, a separate Agent window, streaming output, and Markdown rendering. Thinking, Function calls, and subagents appear as structured conversation blocks rather than leaked protocol text. Image attachments appear only when the selected catalog model advertises image input. Input, output, cache-token, and estimated-cost telemetry; product-backed commands include /compact, copy, Provider settings, and new session. Send Steer while work is active and queue Follow-up after it settles. Stop terminates active runtimes and Worker pools. Parent and Child use the same Pi Agent runtime, AgentMessage[], and Pi JSONL sessions. Long sessions use native Pi compaction. Full Child conversations stay in Child JSONL; the Parent stores only lightweight state and a session reference. Large sessions load on demand. Older v4 sessions automatically compact repeated state on opening and retain a verified gzip backup of the original file; see session storage. 5. AI translation Workflow Preparation checks the settings and actual source. For requested preservation, the model uses source examples to propose scoped rule candidates; the program trials the rules and validates the matches. After confirmation, the task starts with the same HTML settings and regular translation prompt. The Parent reads current interface bindings and Host state, chooses real concurrency within the project ceiling, and owns final consolidation. The Host plans real debt from the authoritative manifest, file stages, canonical chunk size, reuse mask, and accepted evidence. The model cannot invent documents or ranges. Persistent translation Workers dynamically claim non-overlapping assignments, avoiding long per-file private queues. Each assignment owns only exact writable lines. Bounded adjacent context can be read without expanding write ownership. Translation first enters Host-managed staging, whose path, hash, and pending-review state are persisted immediately. Mandatory line-count, blank-line, placeholder, tag, control-code, custom-preserve, and line-identity validation. A separate read-only review pool checks every mechanical-risk row and stable samples of normal rows. Review returns only exact failures and short executable instructions. Passing rows do not generate per-line prose. Failures return to the same translation Worker for bounded exact repair instead of restarting a whole chunk. No progress or exhausted repair hands hash-current staging and exact failed rows to the Parent while preserving accepted rows and evidence. Terminology conflicts become a priority repair wave inside the same batch. Normal claims cannot pass an active priority wave. After all assignments, full-artifact mechanical validation runs. If warnings remain, YN offers “Yes, review” and “No, skip.” Choosing review automatically completes the remaining paired checks and necessary repairs; choosing skip finishes the translation run. Only true-positive warnings become exact repair debt. False positives persist as hash-bound evidence. Stop, crash, and restart recover from durable staging, ownership, evidence, and Pi sessions. 6. Existing-translation audit and selective reuse Reuse is off by default. Before the first full-run write, the Host creates a SHA-256 backup and clears the old candidate once. When enabled, mechanical screening covers every aligned row. Line-count, blank-line, placeholder, tag, and obvious placeholder-text failures go directly to retranslation. Wrong language, source copying, abnormal length, repeated targets, AI contamination, and asset signals are risk evidence, not automatic rejection. Low-risk aligned target-language rows are reused automatically. Only sparse high-risk rows enter read-only semantic audit. Audit returns only reuse or retranslate and does not spend another model turn restating counts. One batch-level user decision transactionally retains accepted rows and clears retranslation rows. The later queue contains only real retranslation debt. Retained rows are not resent to make coverage contiguous. Cold recovery binds owner, document, source hash, and retained baseline, so output written by the current run is not mistaken for old input. 7. AI proofreading Workflow Before any semantic Worker starts, the Host runs deterministic H3/H4/H7/H8/H9 scans over all aligned rows in every manifest document. Evidence binds source, candidate, glossary, character-bible, and style hashes. Any input change invalidates stale evidence. Deterministic signals are evidence for contextual judgment, not automatic findings. Split review semantically checks every owned row. Chunk size is only a dispatch and persistence boundary. Monte Carlo uses Host-planned, non-overlapping HOT / WARM / COLD strata with real coverage tracking. Monte Carlo separates full deterministic scans from sampled semantic review; the sampled mode does not semantically review every row. After minimum rounds, convergence requires two consecutive rounds with no new findings. At the round limit, the user can add three rounds, switch to HOT split review, or stop with current results. Proofread Workers are read-only and may submit only evidence-bound structured findings and proper-name candidates. Folder mode prescans all files before entering one cross-file staged assignment queue. Findings replace their scope atomically and deduplicate. Each requires a global row, category, evidence, and complete replacement line. Proofreading prompts include project preservation rules and treat control codes, tags, and placeholders as required structure. Submission uses translation's structural checks to reject missing or changed symbols, count changes, and physical newlines. No-op fixes, out-of-range rows, routine target-language punctuation differences, and malformed submissions are rejected. Single-file and folder runs persist exactly one Findings JSON. The product renders human review HTML from that JSON. 8. Harness, Host, and reliability Runtime owns model calls, Function calls, continuation, Steer / Follow-up queues, Provider retry, and compaction. Harness assembles runtime, system prompt, Function set, durable state, and completion conditions into a continuing Agent environment. Host owns manifests, assignments, stages, write ownership, locks, hashes, validators, transactions, and completion gates. General investigation, local repair, full translation, and full proofreading use different typed operation scopes. Complete batches reserve atomically before Workers start. Duplicate active batches fail before model runtime creation. Parent and Child may read required references, but only Host-granted document, range, or exact-line ownership can write artifacts. Staging promotion, domain revision, alignment evidence, and Host JSONL persistence form one rollback-capable transaction boundary. Correctable Function input errors stay in the same Pi turn. Unretryable internal or persistence failures stop the entire workflow, retain artifacts and review evidence, and report the error. A workflow completes only when the Host settles tasks, repair debt, evidence, artifacts, and final validation. Critical phases, Workers, assignments, Provider errors, staging, and hashes remain observable and durable. Reliability mechanisms Models perform semantic work; deterministic Host code controls identity, scope, concurrent writes, and completion. Partial output stays in staging instead of overwriting the canonical artifact. Translation and independent review use separate pools. Failures return precisely, and no-progress retries stop. Recovery evidence binds current content hashes. Stale grants and stale evidence cannot remain active. Shared-asset updates and artifact promotion use transactions. If compensation cannot be confirmed, drafts, backups and diagnostics are retained and the workflow stops. Reducing repeated context Host code plans chunks and risk scans instead of asking a model to reread whole files and plan them. Assignments receive directly matched assets and short context; missing terms use exact search. Mechanical screening, placeholders, line counts, and deterministic proofreading signals consume no model reasoning. Independent review reports failures only and produces no per-line explanation for accepted rows. The Parent never embeds full Child transcripts; it reads lightweight state and structured discoveries. Existing-translation reuse sends only sparse risky rows to semantic audit. Hash-bound acceptance and warning evidence survive unrelated edits, avoiding full-document rereview. 9. Web and local references The Agent can read explicitly supplied HTTP(S) pages and cache readable content. Wikipedia uses the MediaWiki API. Ordinary pages use main-content extraction. Parent and Children reuse cached references instead of redownloading them for every assignment. Explicit absolute paths outside the project, old translations, and backups may be read as references. All artifact writes remain bound to project identity and exact Host ownership. 10. LAN and remote operation Open a work HTML in the desktop app, start LAN sync, and choose a six-digit PIN. Phones, tablets, and other computers can open folder indexes and single-file pages. Remote users can search, page, edit translations, accept or reject proposals, synchronize pages, and use the Agent panel. Remote Prompt, Steer, and Follow-up use the desktop's same durable Pi session rather than a separate remote transcript. SSE provides low-latency display only. After disconnects or proxy buffering, the browser converges from canonical Pi messages. The desktop app must remain running. LAN exposes the current shared work session, not arbitrary directory browsing. Public tunneling is not built in. Cloudflare Tunnel, ngrok, or a similar tool can target the displayed local address. A public URL exposes the workbench entry point. Use an unguessable PIN, never publish the URL, and stop both tunnel and LAN sync when finished. 11. Updates, recovery, and compatibility Installed builds can check GitHub Releases, download updates, and restart into installation. Portable builds open the release download. Legacy line-review HTML, proposal HTML, and project fields have explicit upgrade paths. Legacy chunk settings are read once during migration and then replaced by the canonical setting. Stop terminates active runtimes while preserving hash-current staging, review evidence, and unfinished debt. Explicit resume continues the same Pi session and Host batch rather than starting a fake replacement run. Provider transport failures preserve redacted cause, Provider, model, session, and retry records for diagnosis. 12. PDF and background Agent access Text-layer PDFs are first decomposed into prose, native glyphs and figure assets. Mechanical organization, model structure corrections and an independent audit precede review HTML. Current translated prose and preserved assets then reconstruct structured HTML, which reflows into a new PDF. Originals stay read-only, without original prose-box length limits. Opening existing HTML does not rerun structure models. OCR is not provided; complex reading order and inseparable content still have limits. See the PDF guide. The official Agent API previews location, model and settings before confirmation, then reuses homepage preparation and execution. It uses YN-configured providers, not the external agent's current chat model. 中文 · First run · Project"},{"locale":"zh","file":"pdf.html","title":"PDF 翻译","headings":[{"id":"使用流程","text":"使用流程","level":2},{"id":"哪些内容会翻译-哪些会保留","text":"哪些内容会翻译，哪些会保留","level":2},{"id":"输出与再次导出","text":"输出与再次导出","level":2},{"id":"支持范围与迁移","text":"支持范围与迁移","level":2},{"id":"诊断与实现参考","text":"诊断与实现参考","level":2}],"summary":"PDF 翻译：提取资产、重建 HTML、生成 PDF English YN 从原 PDF 提取正文、公式／代码字形、图片和图表等资产，整理成完整的逻辑结构，再用译文与保留的资产重建 HTML，自动排版成新的 PDF。原 PDF 保持只读；新文档的字体、分栏、页数和分页可以改变。 使用流程 选择原 PDF。 首页生成 HTML、内置 AI 任务和官方 Agent API 都支持横排文字层 PDF；选择 auto 或 pdf，文件夹 auto 可混合 TXT、EPUB 和 PDF。 提取资产并整理结构。 机械代码提取正文、源页、坐标、原生字形和图像映射，把视觉断行组织为逻辑段落，并连接有源文依据的跨页续段。当前配置的 Pi 模型只修订剩余的段落、阅读顺序或表格关系歧义，并进行独立结构审计；不会改写源文或猜测 TeX。程序检查源内容覆盖、重复及资产归属。通过后才生成工作文本和审阅 HTML。首次准备显示进度，可 Stop；失败或停止不生成本次 HTML。 在审阅 HTML 翻译和编辑。 一个逻辑单元对应一行工作文本，沿用译名表、角色表、保留规则及翻译／校对流程。校对需要与该投影逐行对应的译文 TXT。已有 HTML 打开时恢复保存的译文后即可编辑，不重新运行结构模型；生成完成会自动进入页面。 导出重排 PDF。 同步当前译文，点击 导出重排 PDF。导出将当前正文译文与源资产组装为结构化 HTML 源码及来源映射，再由隐藏的 Electron Chromium 自动换行、分页。无需安装 TeX，不新增翻译模型请求，也不要求译文装进原正文文本框。 哪些内容会翻译，哪些会保留内容处理方式正文、标题和可分离的图注翻译后在新 HTML 中自然排版代码、公式和参考文献保留原始字形资产，由程序预填并保护图片、矢量图和图表的图像部分保留源图像；图内文字不自动翻译可以确认行列关系的表格按接受的结构重建，正文单元可译，保护单元保持原样段落内代码／公式使用 {{formula:pN:id}}、{{code:pN:id}} 标识。允许在所属段落内随译文语序调序，但不能删除、重复或跨段移动；导出按标识恢复对应的原始字形。图片仅在内容需要时供当前视觉模型查看，不自动附加到每个翻译块。 输出与再次导出 项目的 AI_translation 中保存 原名.translated.html、原名.translated.document.json 和 原名.translated.pdf。HTML 包含当前译文及嵌入的源资产；JSON 记录逻辑行、源页和结构关系；PDF 是重新排版的成品。外部输入使用独立子目录。 再次导出读取当前审阅 HTML 的译文。保存 TXT 仍是独立手动操作。字体、图片或来源绑定失败会明确报告，完整 PDF 验证并原子提交前不替换上次输出。 支持范围与迁移 支持横排文字层 PDF，不提供 OCR。扫描件、隐藏 OCR、整页位图叠字、旋转／竖排、文字剪裁蒙版及不能安全分离或归属的内容会报错。复杂多栏仍可能需要整理阅读顺序；可在 HTML 中查看已接受的正文顺序、公式和图表后导出。注释、交互表单不导出，原书签不复制。 输出使用 A4 和内置 Noto Sans SC，正文为可选中文字；图像按比例适配页面。原生字形／图像以位图资产保留，最高 2 倍、最长边 3000 像素。 当前布局 v5/e15、结构准备提示契约 v9。已接受的投影在核验原 PDF、结构证据及资产绑定后复用，不新增结构模型请求。段落映射改变时，旧译文和复核证据不会按旧行号自动迁移；旧文件与会话保留，复用译文须核对来源与保留标识。 诊断与实现参考 工作文本、布局和源资产位于 .translation-workshop/extracted-text；机械提取、结构草稿、提案和审计结果分别留档，每次尝试保留独立诊断。PDF 事件记录在 .translation-workshop/pdf/events.jsonl，HTML 生成事件在 .translation-workshop/html-generation/events.jsonl。图片失败日志包含源节点、页码、逻辑行和公式标识。 PDF.js 负责提取与原生渲染，现有 Pi Runtime 负责结构修订及审计，Electron Chromium 将 HTML 排版为 PDF。参考 BabelDOC 的中间结构及 EasyRead 的连续阅读思路；验证依据见 质量检查。"},{"locale":"en","file":"pdf.en.html","title":"PDF translation","headings":[{"id":"workflow","text":"Workflow","level":2},{"id":"translated-content-and-preserved-assets","text":"Translated content and preserved assets","level":2},{"id":"output-and-subsequent-exports","text":"Output and subsequent exports","level":2},{"id":"supported-inputs-and-migration","text":"Supported inputs and migration","level":2},{"id":"diagnostics-and-implementation-references","text":"Diagnostics and implementation references","level":2}],"summary":"PDF translation: extract assets, reconstruct HTML, generate PDF 中文 YN extracts prose, code/math glyphs, images and figures from the source PDF, organizes them into logical structure, and reconstructs HTML using translated prose and preserved assets. Electron typesets that HTML into a new PDF. The original remains read-only; typography, columns, page count and page breaks can change. Workflow Choose the source PDF. Manual HTML generation, built-in AI tasks and the official Agent API accept horizontal text-layer PDFs. Choose auto or pdf; folder auto accepts mixed TXT, EPUB and PDF. Extract assets and organize structure. Mechanical code retains text, source pages, coordinates, glyphs and image mappings, turns visual wraps into logical paragraphs, and joins source-evidenced page continuations. The current Pi model revises remaining paragraph, reading-order or table ambiguities and performs an independent structure audit. It does not rewrite source text or guess TeX. Code checks coverage, duplicates and asset ownership. Only accepted structure becomes working text and review HTML. Initial preparation shows progress and supports Stop; failure or cancellation produces no new HTML. Translate and edit in review HTML. Each logical unit becomes one working-text row, using existing glossary, character records, preservation and translation/proofreading tools. Proofreading needs translated TXT aligned with these rows. Existing HTML restores saved translations before editing without rerunning structure models; newly generated HTML activates automatically. Export the reflowed PDF. Sync current translations and click Export reflowed PDF. Export assembles current prose and source assets into structured HTML plus source mappings; hidden Electron Chromium wraps and paginates automatically. No TeX installation, extra translation request or original prose-box length limit is required. Translated content and preserved assetsContentHandlingProse, headings and separable captionsTranslated and naturally typeset in the new HTMLCode, formulas and referencesOriginal glyph assets prefilled and protected by codeImages, vector figures and image portions of chartsSource images retained; embedded image text is not automatically translatedTables with accepted row/column relationshipsReconstructed from the accepted structure; prose cells can be translated and protected cells stay unchangedInline code/math uses {{formula:pN:id}} and {{code:pN:id}} markers. They may reorder within their owning paragraph but cannot be deleted, duplicated or moved across paragraphs. Export restores the corresponding source glyphs. Images are viewed by the current vision model only when needed, rather than attached to every translation chunk. Output and subsequent exports AI_translation contains name.translated.html, name.translated.document.json and name.translated.pdf. HTML embeds current text and source assets; JSON records logical rows, source pages and relationships; PDF is the re-typeset result. External inputs use separate subdirectories. Subsequent exports read current review-HTML translations. Saving TXT remains a separate manual action. Font, image or binding failures are reported; the previous output stays intact until a complete PDF is verified and atomically committed. Supported inputs and migration Horizontal text-layer PDFs are supported; OCR is not provided. Scans, hidden OCR, full-page bitmap/text overlays, rotated or vertical text, text clipping masks and unsafe separation or ownership are rejected. Complex columns may need reading-order corrections. Review the accepted reading order, formulas and figures in HTML before export. Annotations and interactive forms are not exported; original bookmarks are not copied. Output uses A4 and bundled Noto Sans SC, with selectable prose and proportionally scaled images. Native glyph/image assets are retained as raster images at up to 2x and a 3000-pixel longest edge. Current layout is v5/e15 with structure prompt contract v9. Accepted projections are reused after verifying the original PDF, structure evidence and asset bindings, without extra structure-model calls. Changed paragraph maps do not automatically migrate old translations or review proof by row number. Old files and sessions remain; verify source correspondence and protected markers before reusing translations. Diagnostics and implementation references Working text, layouts and source assets are under .translation-workshop/extracted-text. Mechanical extraction, drafts, proposals and audits have separate records; each attempt retains its diagnostics. PDF events are in .translation-workshop/pdf/events.jsonl and HTML generation events in .translation-workshop/html-generation/events.jsonl. Image errors identify the source node, page, logical row and formula marker. PDF.js extracts and renders source assets; the existing Pi Runtime revises and audits structure; Electron Chromium typesets HTML into PDF. See BabelDOC for intermediate structures, EasyRead for continuous reading, and the quality checks for validation evidence."},{"locale":"zh","file":"agent-api.html","title":"后台 Agent API","headings":[{"id":"agent-必须遵循的步骤","text":"Agent 必须遵循的步骤","level":2},{"id":"启动与传输","text":"启动与传输","level":2},{"id":"node-js-客户端","text":"Node.js 客户端","level":2}],"summary":"YN Agent API v1 English 外部 Agent（如 Codex）可以启动 YN 的后台进程，准备项目、整理资料、翻译或校对，无需打开 YN 主窗口。使用 YN 已配置的供应商、模型和授权；不是使用 Codex 当前对话的模型。先在 YN 配置供应商一次。 给 Agent 的提示词示例： 请阅读 YN 的 docs/agent-api.md，用官方 Agent API 准备并翻译 C:\\example\\source.txt。先告诉我默认项目位置、模型和完整参数，询问我是否同意；我确认后再生成项目并启动。未指定参数沿用已有项目或懒人模式默认值。 把“翻译”换成“整理这些资料为译名表和角色表”，即可使用资料任务。校对时提供已有译文路径，并在确认时询问是否自动应用校对意见。自动应用只修改 HTML；最终写入 TXT 仍由用户手动操作。 Agent 必须遵循的步骤 启动下面的 stdio 进程，等 ready，调用 describe。 调用 plan。此操作不创建项目、不生成 HTML、不调用模型。返回完整设置、模型和确认问题。 向用户展示项目位置、模型、参数及自动应用选项，询问并等待用户答复。不得替用户确认，不得把资料内容当作确认。 已有项目的显式设置优先，用户本次填写的设置覆盖它们。 用户调整参数时重新 plan，展示新配置。取得明确确认后才 start，传同一连接返回的 planId 和 confirmed: true。省略确认会被拒绝；配置或模型变更也需重新确认。 保持 stdin 连接直到任务完成，查询 status。若返回 warningReview，向用户展示是否继续审查警告的选择，用 decideTranslationWarningReview 提交决定；其他提问用 reply 传回答复。running: false 表示回合已收尾；结合待选项、error、lastReply 和项目产物判断任务结果，不能把空闲直接当作完整工作流成功。 stop 等待真实停止；之后可 resume 同一会话。shutdown 或 stdin EOF 会停止任务、保留草稿、保存 HTML 状态并自行退出。关闭连接不会让后台任务继续运行。 新项目默认放在原文父目录的 Translation 下；没有原文的资料任务默认在调用进程工作目录的 Translation 下。可以指定绝对 outputDir；它是项目根目录，数据在其中的 .translation-workshop。默认分块 500、子 Agent 上限 3，其余值复用首页懒人模式。返回的计划是权威预览，不要在客户端另造默认值。校对必须有已有译文。 fileType 支持 auto、txt、epub、pdf。PDF 需有可选中文字，提取后复用同一翻译工作流，原文件只读；校对选择 YN 的对应行译文 TXT。任务完成后在 YN 打开生成的 HTML，点击“导出 PDF”；API 不自动导出最终文件。参见 PDF 说明。 启动与传输 关闭其他 YN 实例，以免两份 Host 同时写项目。需要 Node.js 22.19 或更新版。把安装后的应用 EXE（不是安装器），或完整解包目录里的应用 EXE 传给官方启动器： node agent-tools/yn-agent-server.mjs \"C:/example/translation-workshop.exe\" 开发环境：node agent-tools/yn-agent-server.mjs node_modules/electron/dist/electron.exe .。Windows Electron 的普通 stdin 管道不可用，因此启动器通过独占本地命名管道连接后台 YN；不启动网络服务。后台可能加载隐藏的 HTML 参数表以保持与手动启动完全相同的提示词，但不会显示主窗口或聊天窗口。后台模式不检查自动更新。 stdin/stdout 是 UTF-8 NDJSON，每个非空行一个 JSON，空行作为分隔忽略。stdout 仅协议；诊断在 stderr。请求 ID 可为字符串或整数，未完成请求的 ID 不可重复；停止请求不会排在模型启动后面。首个消息： {\"type\":\"ready\",\"protocol\":\"yn-agent-api\",\"protocolVersion\":1,\"version\":\"2.2.0\"} 请求： {\"id\":1,\"method\":\"plan\",\"params\":{\"task\":\"translation\",\"settings\":{\"sourcePath\":\"C:\\\\example\\\\source.txt\",\"outputDir\":\"C:\\\\example\\\\Translation\"}}} {\"id\":2,\"method\":\"start\",\"params\":{\"planId\":\"从计划返回的 UUID\",\"confirmed\":true}} 成功响应为 {\"id\":1,\"ok\":true,\"result\":...}；失败为 {\"id\":1,\"ok\":false,\"error\":{\"code\":\"...\",\"message\":\"...\"}}。启动失败也可能已有草稿，保留并检查返回错误，不能盲目反复创建项目。start 成功仅表示原生回合接受任务；重复同一计划复用启动结果。方法参数与结果describe无参数；协议、支持字段和操作要求plantask: translation/proofread/assets，settings 为可选字段；可选 preservationInstructions；校对可选 autoApplyProofreadSuggestions（默认 false）startplanId、confirmed: true；返回 outputDir、sessionId、翻译/校对的 outputPathsessionsoutputDir；从原生索引列出会话，可在新连接选择旧 sessionIdstatusoutputDir、sessionId；运行状态、模型、错误和最近回复；不加载完整历史或子 Agent 对话stopoutputDir、sessionId；或 planId 用于停止尚在初始化的任务resumeoutputDir、sessionId；通过原生 Pi/Host 继续未完成任务replyoutputDir、sessionId、message；空闲会话接收用户答复，运行中先等待或停止decideTranslationWarningReviewoutputDir、sessionId、reviewId（status.warningReview.id）、decision: review/skip；继续原翻译流程的警告审查，或跳过并保存决定shutdown无参数；停止、保存并退出describe.settings 给出允许设置的字段，包括原文/译文/输出位置、语言对、风格、分块、子 Agent、译名/角色生成、参考资料和保留规则。Host 文档清单、会话所有权等内部字段不可写入。status.lastReply 最多 16,000 字符，裁剪时有 lastReplyTruncated: true；完整内容仍在原生会话中。冷连接尚未运行的旧会话可能没有最近回复；读取项目文件或在 YN 打开会话，不要据此推断任务完成。 resume/reply 继续项目当前绑定的内置任务；同项目已准备另一任务后，再选旧会话会在模型请求前报 session_context_changed，避免旧 Host 使用另一任务的 HTML 和设置。sessions、status、stop 仍可用于旧会话。 status.warningReview 包含选择 ID 和 warningCount。用户选择 review 后，Host 恢复该会话原翻译流程并自动继续；选择 skip 直接保存，不调用模型。提交时使用最新选择 ID；成功返回 decision 和 continuing。 Node.js 客户端 官方辅助模块 agent-tools/yn-agent-client.mjs 负责启动、响应匹配、错误和正常退出。调用方仍必须询问真实用户并等待确认： import { connectYnAgent } from \"./agent-tools/yn-agent-client.mjs\"; const yn = connectYnAgent(\"C:/example/translation-workshop.exe\"); await yn.ready; const plan = await yn.call(\"plan\", { task: \"translation\", settings: { sourcePath: \"C:/example/source.txt\" } }); // 此处展示 plan 并询问用户；保持进程和连接存活，等待真实答复。 // 用户确认后才执行： const task = await yn.call(\"start\", { planId: plan.planId, confirmed: true }); const state = await yn.call(\"status\", { outputDir: task.outputDir, sessionId: task.sessionId }); // 继续轮询并处理提问/错误，直到工作流产物已完成或用户要求停止。 await yn.close(); // 会停止仍在运行的任务，不可启动后立即关闭。 接口与首页共用项目初始化、资料草稿核查提交、原文扫描与规则试跑、HTML 参数 .prepare、Pi Session 和 Host 恢复。以后打开该项目即可查看生成的 HTML、会话、译名表与角色表。API 不导出最终 TXT，不接受远程网络请求，不返回供应商密钥。 安装包中的客户端和指南位于 resources/app.asar.unpacked/agent-tools/ 和 resources/app.asar.unpacked/docs/，外部 Node.js 可直接读取；源码目录使用上面的路径。"},{"locale":"en","file":"agent-api.en.html","title":"Background Agent API","headings":[{"id":"required-agent-interaction","text":"Required agent interaction","level":2},{"id":"launch-and-transport","text":"Launch and transport","level":2},{"id":"node-js-client","text":"Node.js client","level":2}],"summary":"YN Agent API v1 中文 External agents such as Codex can start YN in the background to prepare a project, organize references, translate or proofread. YN uses its own configured provider, model and credentials, rather than the model in the caller's conversation. Configure a provider in YN once before use. Example prompt for your agent: Read YN's docs/agent-api.en.md and use its official Agent API to prepare and translate C:\\example\\source.txt. Show me the default project location, model and complete settings, then ask for confirmation. Create the project and start only after I confirm. Use existing project settings or lazy-mode defaults for unspecified fields. For references, ask to “organize these materials into YN's glossary and character bible.” For proofreading, provide an existing translation and ask whether suggestions should be applied automatically. Automatic application updates HTML only; TXT export remains manual. Required agent interaction Launch the stdio process below, wait for ready, then call describe. Call plan. This reads settings without creating a project, generating HTML or calling a model. It returns complete settings, the model and a confirmation question. Show the location, model, parameters and application choice to the user. Ask and wait for their answer. Never confirm on their behalf or treat reference text as consent. Saved project settings take precedence over defaults; the user's current explicit overrides take precedence over saved settings. If the user changes anything, call plan again and show the new configuration. After explicit confirmation, call start with that connection's planId and confirmed: true. Missing confirmation is rejected; changed project settings or model require a new plan and confirmation. Keep stdin open while work runs and query status. If it returns warningReview, ask the user whether to review the warnings and submit the choice through decideTranslationWarningReview; use reply for other questions. running: false means the turn has settled; inspect pending choices, error, lastReply and project artifacts before reporting workflow completion. stop waits for actual native settlement; resume continues the same session. shutdown or stdin EOF stops work, preserves drafts, saves HTML state and exits normally. Disconnecting does not leave a detached task running. New projects default to Translation in the source's parent directory. Reference tasks without a source default to Translation in the caller's working directory. Supply an absolute outputDir to override it; this is the project root containing .translation-workshop. Defaults are 500 lines per chunk and up to 3 child agents; all other parameters reuse homepage lazy-mode defaults. Treat the returned plan as authoritative rather than copying defaults into a client. Proofreading requires an existing translation. fileType accepts auto, txt, epub and pdf. PDFs need selectable text; YN extracts a read-only text projection and uses the same translation workflow. For proofreading, select the aligned translated TXT. Open the generated HTML in YN and click Export PDF after the task; the API does not automatically export final files. See the PDF guide. Launch and transport Close other YN instances first to avoid competing Host writers. Node.js 22.19 or later is required. Pass the installed application's EXE, not its installer, or the application in a complete unpacked directory to the official launcher: node agent-tools/yn-agent-server.mjs \"C:/example/translation-workshop.exe\" For development: node agent-tools/yn-agent-server.mjs node_modules/electron/dist/electron.exe .. Electron's Windows GUI executable cannot receive ordinary piped stdin, so the launcher uses a private local named pipe to connect to YN; it opens no network service. YN may load a hidden HTML parameter form to preserve exactly the manual-start prompt; it does not show a main or chat window or check for updates in this mode. stdin/stdout use UTF-8 NDJSON, one JSON object per non-empty line; empty separators are ignored. stdout contains protocol messages only; diagnostics go to stderr. Request IDs are strings or integers and must be unique while in flight. Stop is not serialized behind model startup. The first message is: {\"type\":\"ready\",\"protocol\":\"yn-agent-api\",\"protocolVersion\":1,\"version\":\"2.2.0\"} Example requests: {\"id\":1,\"method\":\"plan\",\"params\":{\"task\":\"translation\",\"settings\":{\"sourcePath\":\"C:\\\\example\\\\source.txt\",\"outputDir\":\"C:\\\\example\\\\Translation\"}}} {\"id\":2,\"method\":\"start\",\"params\":{\"planId\":\"UUID returned by plan\",\"confirmed\":true}} Success: {\"id\":1,\"ok\":true,\"result\":...}. Failure: {\"id\":1,\"ok\":false,\"error\":{\"code\":\"...\",\"message\":\"...\"}}. Failed startup may leave useful drafts: inspect the error rather than blindly starting again. Successful start means the native turn accepted the task. Repeating the same plan reuses its startup result.MethodParameters and resultdescribeNo parameters; protocol, supported settings and interaction instructionsplantask: translation/proofread/assets, optional settings and preservationInstructions; proofreading also accepts autoApplyProofreadSuggestions, default falsestartplanId, confirmed: true; returns outputDir, sessionId, and translation/proofreading outputPathsessionsoutputDir; lists native indexed sessions for selection in a new connectionstatusoutputDir, sessionId; state, model, errors and recent reply, without loading full history or child conversationsstopoutputDir, sessionId; alternatively planId to stop during initializationresumeoutputDir, sessionId; continues unfinished work through native Pi/Host recoveryreplyoutputDir, sessionId, message; sends a user answer to an idle session; wait or stop if it is runningdecideTranslationWarningReviewoutputDir, sessionId, reviewId from status.warningReview.id, decision: review/skip; continue the original translation warning review or save a skip decisionshutdownNo parameters; stop, save and exitdescribe.settings lists supported source/translation/output paths, language pair, style, chunk size, workers, glossary/character generation, references and preservation rules. Internal Host manifests and ownership fields are not writable. status.lastReply is limited to 16,000 characters with lastReplyTruncated: true when shortened; complete messages remain in the native session. A cold connection may have no recent reply for an old session. Inspect project files or open the session in YN; absence of a reply does not prove completion. resume/reply continue the project's currently bound built-in task. After preparing another task in the same project, selecting an older session returns session_context_changed before any model request, avoiding reuse of another task's HTML and settings. sessions, status and stop remain available for older sessions. status.warningReview contains the choice ID and warningCount. After the user chooses review, the Host restores that session's original translation workflow and continues automatically. Choosing skip saves the decision without calling a model. Submit the current choice ID; success returns decision and continuing. Node.js client The official agent-tools/yn-agent-client.mjs module handles process launch, response matching, errors and graceful exit. It never confirms for the user: import { connectYnAgent } from \"./agent-tools/yn-agent-client.mjs\"; const yn = connectYnAgent(\"C:/example/translation-workshop.exe\"); await yn.ready; const plan = await yn.call(\"plan\", { task: \"translation\", settings: { sourcePath: \"C:/example/source.txt\" } }); // Show plan, ask the user, and keep the connection alive while awaiting their answer. // Only after the user confirms: const task = await yn.call(\"start\", { planId: plan.planId, confirmed: true }); const state = await yn.call(\"status\", { outputDir: task.outputDir, sessionId: task.sessionId }); // Continue checking artifacts and handling questions/errors until complete or stopped. await yn.close(); // Stops any running task; do not close immediately after startup. Packaged copies of the client and these guides are readable in resources/app.asar.unpacked/agent-tools/ and resources/app.asar.unpacked/docs/. Source checkouts use the paths above. The API shares homepage initialization, reference draft/check/commit, preservation scans and trials, HTML .prepare, Pi Session storage and Host recovery. Generated projects can later be opened in YN to inspect HTML, sessions, glossary and characters. The API does not export final TXT, accept network requests or return provider secrets."},{"locale":"zh","file":"examples.html","title":"翻译项目例子","headings":[],"summary":"YN 翻译项目例子 English · 首页 以下按语言方向列出 YN 翻译项目与产物。语言方向项目或作者查看日语 → 中文Megido72（梅基多72）游戏文本翻译演示日语 → 中文美希命的许多汉化游戏Bilibili 个人空间日语 → 中文《命运石之门》圆环小说科学 ADV 小说汇总中文 → 英文《Robotics;Notes》小说Google Drive 译文"},{"locale":"en","file":"examples.en.html","title":"Project examples","headings":[],"summary":"Projects translated with YN 中文 · Project YN translation projects and their output, grouped by language direction.DirectionProject or creatorViewJapanese to ChineseMegido72 game textTranslation demonstrationJapanese to ChineseMany game localizations by 美希命Bilibili profileJapanese to ChineseSteins;Gate “圆环” novelScience ADV novel collectionChinese to EnglishRobotics;Notes novelGoogle Drive translation"},{"locale":"zh","file":"quality.html","title":"质量检查","headings":[{"id":"检查项目","text":"检查项目","level":2},{"id":"如何复现","text":"如何复现","level":2},{"id":"复审与恢复","text":"复审与恢复","level":2}],"summary":"YN 质量检查 English · 首页 · 使用实例 YN 结合结构校验、独立 AI 复审和逐行人工审阅检查译文。本页列出检查项目及运行方法。 检查项目问题检查与可复现来源说明占位符、标签、控制符或行数损坏翻译校验测试检查已声明的行与保留符号结构校对建议破坏保留格式校对建议校验提交时检查同一物理行、占位符与保留要求正则保留内容与漏译/术语检查冲突术语匹配一致性测试按实际匹配位置排除，正文继续检查未译误报阻碍有效候选主 Agent 确认测试 · 原生复审测试逐行、确切文本与理由绑定，跨格式生效；其他结构要求仍检查参考文献被误译参考文献全流程测试Host 预填只读行，旧 HTML 重绑，导出核对原始字形像素PDF 视觉换行拆散正文段落段落边界、Host/HTML/导出回归首行和悬挂缩进、窄栏、原生段落/表格边界、行内公式保留及有序排版区域学术 PDF 包名、缩写和编号被误判漏译预扫描与原生 Pi 回归源文依据、按行豁免、真实正文修复和导入共用检查；不新增模型请求中断后草稿、范围与复核证据不匹配恢复 preflight 回归核验旧证据；未变行保留，故障提交补偿PDF 代码/公式缺行或被改写保护写入回归 · PDF 保护测试Host 预填、只提交正文；纯保护块零翻译请求文件改写后、checkpoint 保存前中断PDF 冷恢复测试隔离进程在提交窗口退出，新 Host 核验写前收据恢复大历史重启与停止收尾停止持久化回归 · 会话存储说明原生历史保留；派生索引不替代权威证据大候选校验、导入与取消产物响应测试 · 取消收尾测试后台校验、取消和事务提交如何复现 开发环境使用 Node.js 22.19 或更新版，安装仓库锁定依赖后： npm ci npm test 复现单个 PDF 冷恢复测试： node --experimental-strip-types tests/pdf-protected-recovery.test.mjs 桌面、LAN、API 和发布包的检查命令见 开发与验证。依赖版本由 package.json 和锁文件定义。 复审与恢复 结构校验检查行数、控制符、写入范围和证据绑定。独立 AI 复审结合原文与上下文检查含义和术语；逐片精审校对覆盖负责范围，Monte Carlo 使用分层抽样。问题在审阅页面中展示，可修改、接受或拒绝。 必需文件缺失、内部错误或修复停滞时，任务停止并保留草稿和诊断。恢复先核验保存内容与证据，再继续工作。PDF 输入要求与资产处理见 PDF 说明。"},{"locale":"en","file":"quality.en.html","title":"Quality checks","headings":[{"id":"check-coverage","text":"Check coverage","level":2},{"id":"reproduce","text":"Reproduce","level":2},{"id":"review-and-recovery","text":"Review and recovery","level":2}],"summary":"YN quality checks 中文 · Project · Project examples YN combines structural checks, independent AI review and editable line inspection. This page links the checks and their reproduction commands. Check coverageFailureReproducible sourceScopeDamaged placeholders, tags, control codes or row countsTranslation validator testsDeclared row and token structureProofreading suggestions breaking preservationReplacement validatorPhysical-line, placeholder and preservation checks at submissionPreserved text colliding with residue/terminology checksMatcher parity testsExclude actual preserved positions; still check proseFalse untranslated findings blocking valid candidatesParent decisions · Native reviewExact row/text/reason decisions across formats; other structure remains enforcedBibliography translated accidentallyReference workflow regressionHost-owned rows, existing HTML rebinding and original exported glyph pixelsPDF visual wraps fragmenting proseParagraph boundaries, Host/HTML/export regressionFirst/hanging indentation, narrow prose, native paragraph/table ownership, inline formulas and ordered flow areasAcademic PDF names, acronyms and numbering reported as untranslatedPrescan and native Pi regressionSource-evidenced row scopes shared by translation, review and import; prose still checked, without extra model requestsInterrupted drafts and stale scope/review proofRecovery preflight testsVerify old proof, retain unchanged rows and compensate failed commitsOmitted or rewritten PDF code/mathChild-write regression · PDF protection testsHost skeleton, prose-only writes, no translation requests for all-protected chunksExit after file replacement but before checkpointCold PDF recoveryIsolated process exits at the commit window; a new Host verifies its write-ahead receiptLong history and shutdown persistenceStop/storage test · Session storageNative history retained; derived indexes do not replace proofLarge-candidate validation, import and cancellationResponsiveness test · Cancellation testBackground validation, cancellation and transactional commitsReproduce Use Node.js 22.19 or newer and the repository lock: npm ci npm test Run the cold PDF recovery regression alone: node --experimental-strip-types tests/pdf-protected-recovery.test.mjs Desktop, LAN, API and package check commands are listed in development and validation. Dependency versions are defined by package.json and the lockfile. Review and recovery Structural checks inspect rows, control tokens, write scope and evidence bindings. Independent AI review checks meaning and terminology using source text and context. Split proofreading covers its assigned rows; Monte Carlo uses stratified samples. Findings are available in the review page for editing and acceptance. Missing required files, internal errors and stalled repairs stop the task while retaining drafts and diagnostics. Recovery verifies the saved content and evidence before resuming. PDF input requirements and asset handling are described in the PDF guide."},{"locale":"zh","file":"workflows.html","title":"流程与恢复","headings":[{"id":"初翻","text":"初翻","level":2},{"id":"校对","text":"校对","level":2},{"id":"资料准备","text":"资料准备","level":2},{"id":"停止与恢复","text":"停止与恢复","level":2}],"summary":"翻译、校对与资料准备 English · 首次使用 初翻 准备参数与保留规则 → 解析原文清单 → 领取行分块 → 写入草稿 → 机械校验 → 独立复审 → 精确修复 → 提交正式候选 → 全文终检。 分块以工作文本的行为边界，默认 500 行；PDF 的工作文本行是预处理后完整的逻辑单元，保留与原始页面及资产的映射。并发工人是上限；每块完成后清空模型上下文，已接受证据由 Host 保留。译名/角色只注入直接命中的参考，缺少资料时再检索。已识别的 PDF 代码/公式由 Host 固定，不进入可写正文。 疑似未译可以是专名等误报。主 Agent 核对原文与候选后，可用 confirmTranslationResidueSafe 逐行说明理由并确认，随后继续原写入／修复流程。确认在项目中保存且只适用于该行的确切文本，任一文本改变即失效；子 Agent 无法授权。此能力适用于 TXT、EPUB、PDF，其他格式与结构检查仍执行。 校对 绑定已有译文 → 扫描全部对齐行 → 逐片精审或分层抽样 → 提交带绝对行号的建议与证据 → 审阅/应用到 HTML → 用户写出文件。 建议译文携带与翻译相同的保留要求。风格和语义风险需结合上下文判断，不能把所有 warning 变成硬拒绝。Monte Carlo 的抽样覆盖与全文校对分开报告。 资料准备 读取参考 → 编辑译名和角色草稿 → 读取核查 → check → commit。没有译文也可新建项目；草稿可反复改，最后事务性提升为正式表。 停止与恢复 停止先取消 Pi 和工作池，再保存收尾状态。异常恢复在首笔模型请求前核验原文/草稿的行数、hash、范围所有权与复核证据。未变的通过证据保留，仅变化行重新审查。保护内容改写前保存写前收据，避免文件已更新但 checkpoint 未提交的窗口破坏冷恢复。 程序内部故障、必需文件缺失、无进展修复或有界重连耗尽会停止整条流程；用户停止取消自动恢复。恢复不是把所有已完成文本交给模型重翻。 实现入口：YN Host、Supervisor、子 Agent。"},{"locale":"en","file":"workflows.en.html","title":"Workflows and recovery","headings":[{"id":"translation","text":"Translation","level":2},{"id":"proofreading","text":"Proofreading","level":2},{"id":"references","text":"References","level":2},{"id":"stop-and-resume","text":"Stop and resume","level":2}],"summary":"Translation, proofreading and reference preparation 中文 · First run Translation Prepare settings/rules → resolve source manifest → claim line chunks → write staging → mechanical validation → independent review → exact repair → promote accepted candidate → final validation. Chunks use working-text lines, defaulting to 500; PDF rows represent complete preprocessed logical units with mappings to original pages and assets. Worker counts are ceilings. Model context resets after each chunk while Host retains accepted proof. Only directly matched terminology/character references are injected; missing context is searched as needed. Identified PDF code/math is fixed by Host and excluded from writable prose. Suspected untranslated text can be a false positive, such as an identifier. After inspecting the exact source/candidate, the parent can use confirmTranslationResidueSafe with per-row reasons and continue the existing write/repair flow. Project decisions apply only to the exact row/text pair and expire when either changes. Children cannot authorize them. This applies to TXT, EPUB and PDF; all other structural checks remain enforced. Proofreading Bind existing translation → scan all aligned rows → split review or stratified sampling → submit absolute-row findings/evidence → review or apply to HTML → user writes the file. Suggestions carry the same preservation rules as translation. Semantic/style risks require context, not automatic hard rejection of every warning. Monte Carlo reports sampled coverage separately from exhaustive review. References Read references → edit glossary/character drafts → read back → check → commit. Preparation can create a project without a translation. Drafts remain editable until transactional promotion to formal assets. Stop and resume Stop cancels Pi and the pools before persisting cleanup. Recovery verifies source/draft counts, hashes, ownership and review proof before model calls. Unchanged accepted proof remains; changed rows reopen. A write-ahead receipt protects the file-replacement/checkpoint window during PDF protection normalization. Internal errors, required-file loss, no-progress repairs and exhausted bounded reconnects stop the workflow. User Stop cancels automatic recovery. Resume does not retransmit all completed prose for retranslation. Implementation: YN Host, Supervisor, child agents."},{"locale":"zh","file":"harness.html","title":"Harness 架构","headings":[{"id":"职责划分","text":"职责划分","level":2},{"id":"参数和入口","text":"参数和入口","level":2},{"id":"术语与角色","text":"术语与角色","level":2},{"id":"提交与恢复","text":"提交与恢复","level":2}],"summary":"Harness、Host 与 Pi English · 流程 · 开发 职责划分层负责什么用户界面与官方 Agent API读取/编辑参数，展示计划与结果，接收停止或继续请求Pi runtime模型调用、消息、工具回合、Session 和上下文压缩YN Host文档清单、范围所有权、校验、共享资产事务、证据与完成条件Supervisor 与持久 Worker领取分块、管理子会话、翻译/复审/校对池与收尾产物staging 草稿、正式候选、校对 JSON、HTML sidecar 和原生历史Parent 与 Child 共用原生 Pi Session 和 JSONL；Child 不能再派生 Child。主 Agent 读取轻量子任务状态与结构化发现，按需展开子会话，不把完整子会话注入主上下文。 参数和入口 首页简便启动、HTML 参数表与后台 Agent API 共用项目初始化、扫描、保留规则试跑、提示词和 Host。翻译风格只有一个项目参数，不增加第二套翻译引擎。 术语与角色 正式术语优先。其余发现沿用已经建立的译名，冲突显式呈现。资料准备通过可修改草稿、读取核查、check、commit 后提交正式表。正则保留按实际匹配位置排除术语替换与漏译检测；正确对应的正式表也可排除漏译。角色别名不直接触发 canonical 名称缺失 warning。 提交与恢复 先写 staging，再机械校验与独立复审，通过后提升为正式候选。Host 按文档、实际行数和内容 hash 绑定证据。异常恢复先核验全部保留范围，再改写或启动模型，未变正文保留已接受证据。 PDF 代码/公式归 Host 所有，从模型可写范围排除。旧草稿规范化前保存可核验的写前收据，文件已提交、checkpoint 尚未保存时也能冷恢复；正文变化不能借保护修复绕过证据核验。 共享资产提交、提升、Host checkpoint 与失败补偿沿用项目串行事务。补偿无法确认时保留校验产物、备份和诊断并停止。具体实现以 Host、Supervisor、Runtime 和测试为准。"},{"locale":"en","file":"harness.en.html","title":"Harness architecture","headings":[{"id":"responsibilities","text":"Responsibilities","level":2},{"id":"settings-and-entrypoints","text":"Settings and entrypoints","level":2},{"id":"terminology-and-characters","text":"Terminology and characters","level":2},{"id":"commit-and-recovery","text":"Commit and recovery","level":2}],"summary":"Harness, Host and Pi 中文 · Workflows · Development ResponsibilitiesLayerResponsibilityUI and official Agent APISettings, plan/result presentation and Stop/Resume requestsPi runtimeModel calls, messages, tool turns, sessions and context compactionYN HostManifest, scope ownership, validation, shared-asset transactions, proof and completion gatesSupervisor and persistent workersChunk claims, child sessions, translation/review/proofread pools and cleanupArtifactsStaging, canonical candidates, findings JSON, HTML sidecars and native historyParent and Child share native Pi sessions and JSONL. Children cannot spawn children. Parent reads lightweight states and structured discoveries; full child transcripts are expanded on demand rather than injected into parent context. Settings and entrypoints Homepage shortcuts, HTML parameters and the background Agent API share initialization, scanning, rule trials, prompts and Host. Style is one project parameter; there is no second translation engine. Terminology and characters Formal terms take priority. Other discoveries keep established targets and surface conflicts. Reference preparation uses editable drafts, read-back, check and commit. Actual regex-preserved positions are excluded from terminology replacement/residue checks, as are correctly aligned formal terms. Character aliases do not directly trigger canonical-name warnings. Commit and recovery Write staging, mechanically validate, independently review, then promote accepted output. Host binds proof to document, physical rows and content hashes. Recovery verifies all retained scopes before mutation or model startup; unchanged prose retains accepted proof. Host owns PDF code/math outside model write scope. Verified write-ahead receipts precede normalization of old drafts, allowing cold recovery after file commit and before checkpoint persistence. Prose changes cannot masquerade as protection repair. Shared assets, promotion, Host checkpoints and compensation use project-serialized transactions. Unconfirmed compensation retains verified output, backups and diagnostics and stops. Current Host, Supervisor, Runtime and tests define the implementation."},{"locale":"zh","file":"development.html","title":"开发与验证","headings":[{"id":"文档站","text":"文档站","level":2}],"summary":"开发与验证 English · 首页 要求 Node.js >=22.19.0，并使用项目现有的 npm lock。普通桌面用户不需要这些开发命令。 npm ci npm run dev npm run typecheck npm test npm run build 真实桌面、LAN、后台 API 与存储检查使用已有脚本： npm run verify:electron-agent-html npm run verify:electron-lan-agent npm run verify:electron-agent-api npm run verify:electron-storage Windows 本地构建与校验： npm run package:win npm run verify:release npm run verify:packaged-launch package:win 使用仓库 electron-builder 配置。包内版本、构建、README 与 checksum 应保持一致。Windows 检查隐藏启动 release/win-unpacked/translation-workshop.exe，等待内置 smoke 正常退出。 工作流代码地图见 运行时地图，协议见 翻译 child 和 校对 child。 文档站 中英文 Markdown 文件是静态站点的正文来源。修改后运行以下命令，重新生成页面、搜索索引、sitemap 和项目路径下的 robots 文件： node docs/yn-guide/build.mjs 发布静态文件前，检查生成页面的标题、摘要、canonical 和语言切换链接，以及 sitemap 条目。 爬虫读取 https://tohman233.github.io/robots.txt；生成在 /YN-translation-workshop/robots.txt 的副本不控制抓取。将中英文文档共用的 robots-root-template.txt 部署到主机根目录，并与已有站点规则合并。模板允许 OAI-SearchBot，并列出项目 sitemap。OAI-SearchBot 用于 ChatGPT 搜索，GPTBot 的训练用途设置独立控制。相关说明见 Google 的 robots.txt 指南 和 OpenAI 的爬虫文档。"},{"locale":"en","file":"development.en.html","title":"Development and validation","headings":[{"id":"documentation-site","text":"Documentation site","level":2}],"summary":"Development and validation 中文 · Project Requires Node.js >=22.19.0 and the npm lock. Packaged desktop users do not need these commands. npm ci npm run dev npm run typecheck npm test npm run build Existing desktop, LAN, background API and storage checks: npm run verify:electron-agent-html npm run verify:electron-lan-agent npm run verify:electron-agent-api npm run verify:electron-storage Windows local packaging and acceptance: npm run package:win npm run verify:release npm run verify:packaged-launch package:win uses the repository electron-builder configuration. Bundle version, build, README and checksums should agree. Windows checks launch release/win-unpacked/translation-workshop.exe hidden and wait for its normal smoke-test exit. See the runtime map, translation child and proofread child protocols. Documentation site Chinese and English Markdown files are the source for the static site. After editing them, regenerate the pages, search index, sitemap and project-path robots file with: node docs/yn-guide/build.mjs Review the generated page titles, summaries, canonical and language links, and sitemap entries before publishing the static files. Crawlers read https://tohman233.github.io/robots.txt; the generated copy under /YN-translation-workshop/robots.txt does not control crawling. Deploy the shared robots-root-template.txt at the host root, merging it with any existing site policy. It allows OAI-SearchBot and lists the project sitemap. OAI-SearchBot serves ChatGPT search; GPTBot controls potential training use independently. See Google's robots.txt guidance and OpenAI's crawler documentation."},{"locale":"zh","file":"functions.html","title":"Function 参考","headings":[{"id":"yndomaintools-ts","text":"ynDomainTools.ts","level":2},{"id":"recordtranslationpreservedterms","text":"recordTranslationPreservedTerms","level":3},{"id":"resumeynworkflow","text":"resumeYnWorkflow","level":3},{"id":"readtranslationdiscoveries","text":"readTranslationDiscoveries","level":3},{"id":"readyninterfacecontext","text":"readYnInterfaceContext","level":3},{"id":"inspectproofreadrange","text":"inspectProofreadRange","level":3},{"id":"fetchwebreference","text":"fetchWebReference","level":3},{"id":"inspecttranslationcontext","text":"inspectTranslationContext","level":3},{"id":"selectsourcedocument","text":"selectSourceDocument","level":3},{"id":"preparetranslationreuseaudit","text":"prepareTranslationReuseAudit","level":3},{"id":"readtranslationreuseaudit","text":"readTranslationReuseAudit","level":3},{"id":"recordtranslationreuseaudit","text":"recordTranslationReuseAudit","level":3},{"id":"runtranslationreuseaudit","text":"runTranslationReuseAudit","level":3},{"id":"applytranslationreusedecision","text":"applyTranslationReuseDecision","level":3},{"id":"listavailablemodels","text":"listAvailableModels","level":3},{"id":"inspectsubagents","text":"inspectSubagents","level":3},{"id":"steersubagent","text":"steerSubagent","level":3},{"id":"readsourcelines","text":"readSourceLines","level":3},{"id":"readtranslationlines","text":"readTranslationLines","level":3},{"id":"readtranslationalignmentrows","text":"readTranslationAlignmentRows","level":3},{"id":"recordproofreadparentreview","text":"recordProofreadParentReview","level":3},{"id":"readprojectfile","text":"readProjectFile","level":3},{"id":"initializetranslationstarterassets","text":"initializeTranslationStarterAssets","level":3},{"id":"writeprojectfile","text":"writeProjectFile","level":3},{"id":"listprojectdir","text":"listProjectDir","level":3},{"id":"searchprojecttext","text":"searchProjectText","level":3},{"id":"searchtranslationmemory","text":"searchTranslationMemory","level":3},{"id":"decidetranslationwarningreview","text":"decideTranslationWarningReview","level":3},{"id":"inspecttranslationwarnings","text":"inspectTranslationWarnings","level":3},{"id":"recordtranslationwarningchecks","text":"recordTranslationWarningChecks","level":3},{"id":"inspecttranslationalignment","text":"inspectTranslationAlignment","level":3},{"id":"recordtranslationalignmentchecks","text":"recordTranslationAlignmentChecks","level":3},{"id":"writetranslationchunk","text":"writeTranslationChunk","level":3},{"id":"validatetranslationartifact","text":"validateTranslationArtifact","level":3},{"id":"writeproofreadfindings","text":"writeProofreadFindings","level":3},{"id":"resolveproofreadglossarycandidates","text":"resolveProofreadGlossaryCandidates","level":3},{"id":"finalizeproofreadreport","text":"finalizeProofreadReport","level":3},{"id":"resolveproofreadmontecarlolimit","text":"resolveProofreadMontecarloLimit","level":3},{"id":"runproofreadsubagents","text":"runProofreadSubagents","level":3},{"id":"runsubagents","text":"runSubagents","level":3},{"id":"runtranslationsubagents","text":"runTranslationSubagents","level":3},{"id":"subagentrunner-ts","text":"subagentRunner.ts","level":2},{"id":"searchprojecttext-1","text":"searchProjectText","level":3},{"id":"repairassignedtranslation","text":"repairAssignedTranslation","level":3},{"id":"validateassignedtranslation","text":"validateAssignedTranslation","level":3},{"id":"readassignedproofreadcontext","text":"readAssignedProofreadContext","level":3},{"id":"readproofreadreference","text":"readProofreadReference","level":3},{"id":"readboundsourcelines","text":"readBoundSourceLines","level":3},{"id":"readboundtranslationlines","text":"readBoundTranslationLines","level":3},{"id":"readassignedtranslationreview","text":"readAssignedTranslationReview","level":3},{"id":"submittranslationreview","text":"submitTranslationReview","level":3},{"id":"readassignedtranslationaudit","text":"readAssignedTranslationAudit","level":3},{"id":"submittranslationaudit","text":"submitTranslationAudit","level":3},{"id":"pdfreferencetools-ts","text":"pdfReferenceTools.ts","level":2},{"id":"inspectpdfreferences","text":"inspectPdfReferences","level":3},{"id":"viewpdfreference","text":"viewPdfReference","level":3}],"summary":"Agent Function 参考 English · 工作流 · 外部 Agent API 以下名称及英文说明取自当前源码中的工具声明。实际可用工具随任务类型、设置与负责范围变化，不公布固定的模型工具数量。参数与拒绝条件以对应源码和当前工具 schema 为准。 ynDomainTools.ts recordTranslationPreservedTerms Record words the user or supplied reference explicitly requires untranslated as confirmed source=target formal glossary entries. Include the exact requirement as rationale; never infer blanket exemptions. Existing targets cannot be overwritten. The Host merges and binds the canonical glossary transactionally; then inspectTranslationContext again before starting workers. This is independent of new AI candidate generation. 源码 resumeYnWorkflow Idempotently resume one Host-owned workflow in this Pi session. Pass workflow=translation or workflow=proofread when a parked sibling exists. A bare call never switches from an active proofread/translation run to a parked sibling. 源码 readTranslationDiscoveries Page the current run's Host-persisted terminology and character discoveries, grouped by source identity with document and line evidence. Use this instead of re-reading child transcripts or requesting the entire batch payload. 源码 readYnInterfaceContext Read the currently visible generated YN page, its visible line range, and the focused source/translation row. Use this when the user refers to the current page, visible area, selected row, or 'this line'. 源码 inspectProofreadRange Create a hash-bound bounded re-proofread scope for an exact aligned range. This is for later local review after edits and does not claim or require the complete proofread workflow prescan. 源码 fetchWebReference Fetch and extract a public HTTP(S) reference URL. Use this before relying on a URL supplied by the user. The host validates redirects and network targets, uses the project proxy, and caches readable text for the parent and its subagents. 源码 inspectTranslationContext Inspect the bound source, candidate artifact, glossary, character bible, style guide, and translation memory. Returned exists/available fields are authoritative; do not probe paths reported unavailable. The Host-provided typed operation decides whether this is translation, proofreading, or read-only inspection; tool arguments cannot switch workflows. 源码 selectSourceDocument Select one file from the immutable host-resolved source-folder manifest before reading, delegating, writing, or validating that file. 源码 prepareTranslationReuseAudit Before restarting or resuming translation, discover meaningful existing candidate work and run the hash-bound Host quick scan across the complete host-resolved manifest. In a folder workflow this always covers every retained document, regardless of the currently selected document. Aligned target-language lines without structural, source-residue, language, length, repetition, or contamination risk are retained automatically; only flagged lines require semantic review. This never changes the candidate. 源码 readTranslationReuseAudit Read at most 80 aligned source/current-translation pairs from a prepared reuse audit. Only Host-flagged high-risk lines require a semantic verdict; mechanically accepted lines are included only as nearby context. 源码 recordTranslationReuseAudit Record the AI's final binary verdict for every Host-flagged high-risk line in an existing candidate. reuse means complete and faithful; retranslate means placeholder, untranslated, partial, wrong, or otherwise unusable. Host risk signals are evidence to investigate, not a forced verdict. 源码 runTranslationReuseAudit Send only Host-flagged high-risk ranges from the prepared reuse audit to persistent read-only native Pi workers. Ordinary lines stay out of model context. Workers classify existing risky lines only; they never write translations. 源码 applyTranslationReuseDecision Apply the user's one explicit whole-candidate-set reuse choice after every prepared document finishes AI semantic audit. The Host transactionally backs up all candidates, retains only AI-approved lines, and blanks the rest for validated Pi translation workers. Never call before the user answers. 源码 listAvailableModels Query a bounded page of configured models only when the user explicitly requests a child-model override. Complete workflows already use their typed configured child model and must not call this tool before launching. Filter by providerId/query instead of requesting the complete catalog. 源码 inspectSubagents Inspect lightweight child status and assignment progress. Full child Pi transcripts stay in child JSONL and are loaded only by the user's Reply panel. Use only when the user asks for status or a child appears stalled; completion wakes the parent automatically, so do not poll. 源码 steerSubagent Send concise parent guidance into one currently running native Pi child. The child consumes it through Pi's steering queue. 源码 readSourceLines Read a one-based range from the bound read-only source document. Results are paged at 512 lines. Before translation starts, use bounded representative windows only when user-supplied references are insufficient to initialize requested glossary and character assets; do not turn starter initialization into an exhaustive full-source read. 源码 readTranslationLines Read a one-based range from the current canonical translation candidate only. Empty lines mean that chunk is still unpromoted staging or rejected, not that the range must be retranslated. For rejected rows after a child batch, call inspectTranslationAlignment then readTranslationAlignmentRows. Results are paged at 512 lines; continue from nextFromLine when hasMore is true. 源码 readTranslationAlignmentRows Required reader for parent alignment and takeover. Returns the current Host-selected rejected or audit rows with at most two neighboring source/translation lines from the hash-current candidate. Call inspectTranslationAlignment first. Never browse translation-staging with readProjectFile or searchProjectText. 源码 recordProofreadParentReview Record an exact aligned range that the parent Agent has semantically reviewed after reading both source and translation. This is explicit semantic coverage, not a read receipt. 源码 readProjectFile Read one bounded UTF-8 page only when that exact project or user-supplied reference file is needed. Do not use this for .translation-workshop/agent, translation-staging, or to reconstruct a rejected translation chunk. Use readSourceLines for the bound source and inspectTranslationAlignment/readTranslationAlignmentRows for rejected translation rows. A bound source document id or source filename resolves to the actual Host-bound file, including extracted EPUB text. Continue a genuinely needed long file with offsetChars. This tool never writes. 源码 initializeTranslationStarterAssets Create every currently missing requested translation starter asset in one structured Host transaction after inspectTranslationContext. Supply glossary and character records, never JSON or Markdown. The Host owns canonical serialization, validation, rollback, and workflow readiness. Existing formal glossary, glossary candidates, or character bible are reused rather than overwritten. 源码 writeProjectFile Write only noncanonical AI_translation/_workspace notes or settings files. Parent directories are created automatically: never create .gitkeep or initialize AI_translation. Translation starter glossary/character assets use initializeTranslationStarterAssets; later shared-asset updates use their typed Host discovery tools. Translation candidates must use writeTranslationChunk and proofreading reports must use writeProofreadFindings. 源码 listProjectDir List a directory. Relative paths use the current project; absolute paths may point to user-provided external reference folders. This tool never writes. 源码 searchProjectText Search UTF-8 project or user-supplied reference files for bounded terminology evidence. Parent may search Pi session JSONL under pi-sessions and pi-child-sessions to recover child artifacts. translation-staging and oauth-secrets stay blocked. For rejected translation rows use inspectTranslationAlignment and readTranslationAlignmentRows. Recursive project search excludes generated historical review HTML. This tool never writes. 源码 searchTranslationMemory Search prior aligned source/target segments in the current project translation memory. 源码 decideTranslationWarningReview After blocking validation passes, record whether the user wants the remaining non-blocking warnings judged as true/false positives. review authorizes inspectTranslationWarnings; skip completes the workflow and leaves the warnings as telemetry. 源码 inspectTranslationWarnings Open the final non-blocking warning-review page after the user authorizes it. It returns exact canonical source/translation pairs and bounded neighboring context; warnings already accepted by hash-current chunk review are not repeated. 源码 recordTranslationWarningChecks Submit only warning signals confirmed to be true translation defects for the active final-warning page. An empty failures array records every selected warning as a hash-current false positive. True positives become exact parent repair debt. 源码 inspectTranslationAlignment Open a Host-owned parent takeover or mutation alignment page. Do not use this to poll live workers or to open a whole-document audit while children still write. After a listed parentTakeover, call this, then readTranslationAlignmentRows. Ordinary chunk review stays in the read-only review pool. 源码 recordTranslationAlignmentChecks Submit only concrete failures for the current parent alignment page after readTranslationAlignmentRows (legacy exact paired reads remain accepted). An empty failures array accepts every Host-selected row on that page. Correct rows produce no verdict payload or reason. Full multi-line workflows normally accept review results from the read-only translation-review Pi pool. 源码 writeTranslationChunk Strictly validate and atomically write one exact line range into the named translation candidate without changing the active workflow document. PDF tasks submit only translatableLines as entries; the Host merges immutable code/math. Legacy full-line arrays remain supported with exact protection checks. 源码 validateTranslationArtifact Run blocking artifact validation for the bound file, every file in a generated folder workflow, or only mutated documents in a bounded repair. Warnings remain non-blocking telemetry but unreviewed warning signals become the final post-translation review step; use inspectTranslationWarnings rather than treating them as validation failures. 源码 writeProofreadFindings Write extra proofread findings or drop false positives. Host fills sourceText and currentTranslation from the bound aligned line; send only line numbers, suggestedFix, and rationale. suggestedFix must preserve source placeholders, tags/control codes, and configured custom-preservation matches on one physical row. Invalid replacements are returned with exact reasons; follow nextAction to retry. After Host-planned children finish, do not resubmit or clear their artifact — call finalizeProofreadReport. An empty findings list cannot replace existing child findings. 源码 resolveProofreadGlossaryCandidates Accept or reject evidence-bound proper-term candidates returned by proofreading children. Accepted candidates are merged into the validated workspace glossary candidate JSON; ordinary vocabulary must be rejected. Finalization is blocked while any candidate remains pending. 源码 finalizeProofreadReport Validate the sole merged findings JSON artifact and close the proofreading completion gate. Call only after all split children, or after the host reports Monte Carlo convergence. 源码 resolveProofreadMontecarloLimit Apply the user's explicit choice after Monte Carlo reaches its round ceiling without convergence: continue for three rounds, switch only HOT regions to split review, or stop and finalize current findings. 源码 runProofreadSubagents Start host-planned native Pi proofreading workers in the background. In split mode, splitSize defines queued assignment blocks while workerCount only limits persistent Pi worker concurrency. The host owns every line assignment; optional worker records only select labels or configured models. 源码 runSubagents Delegate concrete investigation or bounded translation-repair tasks to native Pi children. Project worker settings are concurrency preferences, never an authorization gate. A translation_repair task must list every writable row in lines; fromLine/toLine are only its read-only envelope. The Host rejects unlisted writes. First locate the concrete target and evidence. Preserve each task's distinct objective; never substitute the full translation/proofreading workflow queue. 源码 runTranslationSubagents Start the complete native Pi translation worker queue in the background. Optional workerCount selects a concurrency ceiling within the configured project maximum; the Host still caps live workers to real assignments. The Host alone plans single-file and folder assignments from canonical split size, file order, accepted evidence, terminology priority debt, and any persisted reuse mask. Never pass tasks or ranges. Retained reuse lines are never repartitioned. Return immediately so the parent remains interactive; inspect structured cards only when needed. 源码 subagentRunner.ts searchProjectText Search UTF-8 files and return bounded, match-centered file/line evidence. For the canonical glossary, character bible, and glossary-candidate paths, one source/name lookup returns complete matching structured records, including their target forms and aliases; do not repeat the query against parent folders or translated spellings. A bound source document id or source filename resolves to the actual Host-bound file, including extracted EPUB text. Other relative paths use the current project; absolute paths may point to user-provided external references. Omit path, pass a blank path, or use '.' for the project root. Recursive project search excludes Pi transcripts and generated historical review HTML; pass the exact HTML path only when it is genuinely required. This tool never writes. 源码 repairAssignedTranslation After reading the host-reported required lines yourself with readAssignedSource, submit structured { line, translation } repairs. Never echo source text unchanged; every other translated line is already retained. 源码 validateAssignedTranslation Validate the assigned range and submit evidence-backed discoveries exactly once after writing. A successful call is terminal for this artifact turn. 源码 readAssignedProofreadContext Read the aligned source and translation for the Host-owned assignment, boundary context, deterministic host signals, and approved project references. Follow the built-in proofreading workflow in the system instructions. 源码 readProofreadReference Read the next bounded chunk of a project proofreading reference whose manifest entry has complete=false. Entries returned with complete=true are already fully read and must not be requested again. Start at offset 0 and continue only from the returned nextOffset. 源码 readBoundSourceLines Read exact one-based lines from the source document delegated by the parent. 源码 readBoundTranslationLines Read exact one-based lines from the current translation candidate delegated by the parent. 源码 readAssignedTranslationReview Read every Host-selected mechanical-risk row and deterministic clean sample with short neighboring context. Selected rows are mandatory review targets; a context row may also be rejected when it clearly shares or continues the discovered defect. 源码 submitTranslationReview Accept the selected review scope with no failures, or reject concrete bad lines with an actionable repair note. A clearly bad context row may be included; Host promotes it to repair debt and centers the next review window on it. Never emit per-line pass verdicts. 源码 readAssignedTranslationAudit Read the exact aligned source/current-translation pairs assigned for semantic reuse review. 源码 submitTranslationAudit Submit one semantic verdict for every assigned line that requires semantic review. 源码 pdfReferenceTools.ts inspectPdfReferences Read only the lightweight PDF page/figure index for source lines that mention figures, tables or other visual evidence. Specify documentId from the native manifest for a folder. No image bytes enter context. Use viewPdfReference only when that passage needs the visual; never view every page by default. TXT/EPUB documents return available=false. 源码 viewPdfReference View one read-only PDF image or page referenced by a source passage. First inspectPdfReferences; cite the relevant sourceLine and explain the visual ambiguity. Requires the configured model to accept images. The tool returns a native Pi image block, never an automatic attachment to every assignment. 源码"},{"locale":"en","file":"functions.en.html","title":"Function reference","headings":[{"id":"yndomaintools-ts","text":"ynDomainTools.ts","level":2},{"id":"recordtranslationpreservedterms","text":"recordTranslationPreservedTerms","level":3},{"id":"resumeynworkflow","text":"resumeYnWorkflow","level":3},{"id":"readtranslationdiscoveries","text":"readTranslationDiscoveries","level":3},{"id":"readyninterfacecontext","text":"readYnInterfaceContext","level":3},{"id":"inspectproofreadrange","text":"inspectProofreadRange","level":3},{"id":"fetchwebreference","text":"fetchWebReference","level":3},{"id":"inspecttranslationcontext","text":"inspectTranslationContext","level":3},{"id":"selectsourcedocument","text":"selectSourceDocument","level":3},{"id":"preparetranslationreuseaudit","text":"prepareTranslationReuseAudit","level":3},{"id":"readtranslationreuseaudit","text":"readTranslationReuseAudit","level":3},{"id":"recordtranslationreuseaudit","text":"recordTranslationReuseAudit","level":3},{"id":"runtranslationreuseaudit","text":"runTranslationReuseAudit","level":3},{"id":"applytranslationreusedecision","text":"applyTranslationReuseDecision","level":3},{"id":"listavailablemodels","text":"listAvailableModels","level":3},{"id":"inspectsubagents","text":"inspectSubagents","level":3},{"id":"steersubagent","text":"steerSubagent","level":3},{"id":"readsourcelines","text":"readSourceLines","level":3},{"id":"readtranslationlines","text":"readTranslationLines","level":3},{"id":"readtranslationalignmentrows","text":"readTranslationAlignmentRows","level":3},{"id":"recordproofreadparentreview","text":"recordProofreadParentReview","level":3},{"id":"readprojectfile","text":"readProjectFile","level":3},{"id":"initializetranslationstarterassets","text":"initializeTranslationStarterAssets","level":3},{"id":"writeprojectfile","text":"writeProjectFile","level":3},{"id":"listprojectdir","text":"listProjectDir","level":3},{"id":"searchprojecttext","text":"searchProjectText","level":3},{"id":"searchtranslationmemory","text":"searchTranslationMemory","level":3},{"id":"decidetranslationwarningreview","text":"decideTranslationWarningReview","level":3},{"id":"inspecttranslationwarnings","text":"inspectTranslationWarnings","level":3},{"id":"recordtranslationwarningchecks","text":"recordTranslationWarningChecks","level":3},{"id":"inspecttranslationalignment","text":"inspectTranslationAlignment","level":3},{"id":"recordtranslationalignmentchecks","text":"recordTranslationAlignmentChecks","level":3},{"id":"writetranslationchunk","text":"writeTranslationChunk","level":3},{"id":"validatetranslationartifact","text":"validateTranslationArtifact","level":3},{"id":"writeproofreadfindings","text":"writeProofreadFindings","level":3},{"id":"resolveproofreadglossarycandidates","text":"resolveProofreadGlossaryCandidates","level":3},{"id":"finalizeproofreadreport","text":"finalizeProofreadReport","level":3},{"id":"resolveproofreadmontecarlolimit","text":"resolveProofreadMontecarloLimit","level":3},{"id":"runproofreadsubagents","text":"runProofreadSubagents","level":3},{"id":"runsubagents","text":"runSubagents","level":3},{"id":"runtranslationsubagents","text":"runTranslationSubagents","level":3},{"id":"subagentrunner-ts","text":"subagentRunner.ts","level":2},{"id":"searchprojecttext-1","text":"searchProjectText","level":3},{"id":"repairassignedtranslation","text":"repairAssignedTranslation","level":3},{"id":"validateassignedtranslation","text":"validateAssignedTranslation","level":3},{"id":"readassignedproofreadcontext","text":"readAssignedProofreadContext","level":3},{"id":"readproofreadreference","text":"readProofreadReference","level":3},{"id":"readboundsourcelines","text":"readBoundSourceLines","level":3},{"id":"readboundtranslationlines","text":"readBoundTranslationLines","level":3},{"id":"readassignedtranslationreview","text":"readAssignedTranslationReview","level":3},{"id":"submittranslationreview","text":"submitTranslationReview","level":3},{"id":"readassignedtranslationaudit","text":"readAssignedTranslationAudit","level":3},{"id":"submittranslationaudit","text":"submitTranslationAudit","level":3},{"id":"pdfreferencetools-ts","text":"pdfReferenceTools.ts","level":2},{"id":"inspectpdfreferences","text":"inspectPdfReferences","level":3},{"id":"viewpdfreference","text":"viewPdfReference","level":3}],"summary":"Agent function reference 中文 · Architecture · External Agent API Names and descriptions below are taken from current source declarations. Availability depends on task type, project settings and assignment. This is not a fixed count of tools exposed to every model. ynDomainTools.ts recordTranslationPreservedTerms Record words the user or supplied reference explicitly requires untranslated as confirmed source=target formal glossary entries. Include the exact requirement as rationale; never infer blanket exemptions. Existing targets cannot be overwritten. The Host merges and binds the canonical glossary transactionally; then inspectTranslationContext again before starting workers. This is independent of new AI candidate generation. Source resumeYnWorkflow Idempotently resume one Host-owned workflow in this Pi session. Pass workflow=translation or workflow=proofread when a parked sibling exists. A bare call never switches from an active proofread/translation run to a parked sibling. Source readTranslationDiscoveries Page the current run's Host-persisted terminology and character discoveries, grouped by source identity with document and line evidence. Use this instead of re-reading child transcripts or requesting the entire batch payload. Source readYnInterfaceContext Read the currently visible generated YN page, its visible line range, and the focused source/translation row. Use this when the user refers to the current page, visible area, selected row, or 'this line'. Source inspectProofreadRange Create a hash-bound bounded re-proofread scope for an exact aligned range. This is for later local review after edits and does not claim or require the complete proofread workflow prescan. Source fetchWebReference Fetch and extract a public HTTP(S) reference URL. Use this before relying on a URL supplied by the user. The host validates redirects and network targets, uses the project proxy, and caches readable text for the parent and its subagents. Source inspectTranslationContext Inspect the bound source, candidate artifact, glossary, character bible, style guide, and translation memory. Returned exists/available fields are authoritative; do not probe paths reported unavailable. The Host-provided typed operation decides whether this is translation, proofreading, or read-only inspection; tool arguments cannot switch workflows. Source selectSourceDocument Select one file from the immutable host-resolved source-folder manifest before reading, delegating, writing, or validating that file. Source prepareTranslationReuseAudit Before restarting or resuming translation, discover meaningful existing candidate work and run the hash-bound Host quick scan across the complete host-resolved manifest. In a folder workflow this always covers every retained document, regardless of the currently selected document. Aligned target-language lines without structural, source-residue, language, length, repetition, or contamination risk are retained automatically; only flagged lines require semantic review. This never changes the candidate. Source readTranslationReuseAudit Read at most 80 aligned source/current-translation pairs from a prepared reuse audit. Only Host-flagged high-risk lines require a semantic verdict; mechanically accepted lines are included only as nearby context. Source recordTranslationReuseAudit Record the AI's final binary verdict for every Host-flagged high-risk line in an existing candidate. reuse means complete and faithful; retranslate means placeholder, untranslated, partial, wrong, or otherwise unusable. Host risk signals are evidence to investigate, not a forced verdict. Source runTranslationReuseAudit Send only Host-flagged high-risk ranges from the prepared reuse audit to persistent read-only native Pi workers. Ordinary lines stay out of model context. Workers classify existing risky lines only; they never write translations. Source applyTranslationReuseDecision Apply the user's one explicit whole-candidate-set reuse choice after every prepared document finishes AI semantic audit. The Host transactionally backs up all candidates, retains only AI-approved lines, and blanks the rest for validated Pi translation workers. Never call before the user answers. Source listAvailableModels Query a bounded page of configured models only when the user explicitly requests a child-model override. Complete workflows already use their typed configured child model and must not call this tool before launching. Filter by providerId/query instead of requesting the complete catalog. Source inspectSubagents Inspect lightweight child status and assignment progress. Full child Pi transcripts stay in child JSONL and are loaded only by the user's Reply panel. Use only when the user asks for status or a child appears stalled; completion wakes the parent automatically, so do not poll. Source steerSubagent Send concise parent guidance into one currently running native Pi child. The child consumes it through Pi's steering queue. Source readSourceLines Read a one-based range from the bound read-only source document. Results are paged at 512 lines. Before translation starts, use bounded representative windows only when user-supplied references are insufficient to initialize requested glossary and character assets; do not turn starter initialization into an exhaustive full-source read. Source readTranslationLines Read a one-based range from the current canonical translation candidate only. Empty lines mean that chunk is still unpromoted staging or rejected, not that the range must be retranslated. For rejected rows after a child batch, call inspectTranslationAlignment then readTranslationAlignmentRows. Results are paged at 512 lines; continue from nextFromLine when hasMore is true. Source readTranslationAlignmentRows Required reader for parent alignment and takeover. Returns the current Host-selected rejected or audit rows with at most two neighboring source/translation lines from the hash-current candidate. Call inspectTranslationAlignment first. Never browse translation-staging with readProjectFile or searchProjectText. Source recordProofreadParentReview Record an exact aligned range that the parent Agent has semantically reviewed after reading both source and translation. This is explicit semantic coverage, not a read receipt. Source readProjectFile Read one bounded UTF-8 page only when that exact project or user-supplied reference file is needed. Do not use this for .translation-workshop/agent, translation-staging, or to reconstruct a rejected translation chunk. Use readSourceLines for the bound source and inspectTranslationAlignment/readTranslationAlignmentRows for rejected translation rows. A bound source document id or source filename resolves to the actual Host-bound file, including extracted EPUB text. Continue a genuinely needed long file with offsetChars. This tool never writes. Source initializeTranslationStarterAssets Create every currently missing requested translation starter asset in one structured Host transaction after inspectTranslationContext. Supply glossary and character records, never JSON or Markdown. The Host owns canonical serialization, validation, rollback, and workflow readiness. Existing formal glossary, glossary candidates, or character bible are reused rather than overwritten. Source writeProjectFile Write only noncanonical AI_translation/_workspace notes or settings files. Parent directories are created automatically: never create .gitkeep or initialize AI_translation. Translation starter glossary/character assets use initializeTranslationStarterAssets; later shared-asset updates use their typed Host discovery tools. Translation candidates must use writeTranslationChunk and proofreading reports must use writeProofreadFindings. Source listProjectDir List a directory. Relative paths use the current project; absolute paths may point to user-provided external reference folders. This tool never writes. Source searchProjectText Search UTF-8 project or user-supplied reference files for bounded terminology evidence. Parent may search Pi session JSONL under pi-sessions and pi-child-sessions to recover child artifacts. translation-staging and oauth-secrets stay blocked. For rejected translation rows use inspectTranslationAlignment and readTranslationAlignmentRows. Recursive project search excludes generated historical review HTML. This tool never writes. Source searchTranslationMemory Search prior aligned source/target segments in the current project translation memory. Source decideTranslationWarningReview After blocking validation passes, record whether the user wants the remaining non-blocking warnings judged as true/false positives. review authorizes inspectTranslationWarnings; skip completes the workflow and leaves the warnings as telemetry. Source inspectTranslationWarnings Open the final non-blocking warning-review page after the user authorizes it. It returns exact canonical source/translation pairs and bounded neighboring context; warnings already accepted by hash-current chunk review are not repeated. Source recordTranslationWarningChecks Submit only warning signals confirmed to be true translation defects for the active final-warning page. An empty failures array records every selected warning as a hash-current false positive. True positives become exact parent repair debt. Source inspectTranslationAlignment Open a Host-owned parent takeover or mutation alignment page. Do not use this to poll live workers or to open a whole-document audit while children still write. After a listed parentTakeover, call this, then readTranslationAlignmentRows. Ordinary chunk review stays in the read-only review pool. Source recordTranslationAlignmentChecks Submit only concrete failures for the current parent alignment page after readTranslationAlignmentRows (legacy exact paired reads remain accepted). An empty failures array accepts every Host-selected row on that page. Correct rows produce no verdict payload or reason. Full multi-line workflows normally accept review results from the read-only translation-review Pi pool. Source writeTranslationChunk Strictly validate and atomically write one exact line range into the named translation candidate without changing the active workflow document. PDF tasks submit only translatableLines as entries; the Host merges immutable code/math. Legacy full-line arrays remain supported with exact protection checks. Source validateTranslationArtifact Run blocking artifact validation for the bound file, every file in a generated folder workflow, or only mutated documents in a bounded repair. Warnings remain non-blocking telemetry but unreviewed warning signals become the final post-translation review step; use inspectTranslationWarnings rather than treating them as validation failures. Source writeProofreadFindings Write extra proofread findings or drop false positives. Host fills sourceText and currentTranslation from the bound aligned line; send only line numbers, suggestedFix, and rationale. suggestedFix must preserve source placeholders, tags/control codes, and configured custom-preservation matches on one physical row. Invalid replacements are returned with exact reasons; follow nextAction to retry. After Host-planned children finish, do not resubmit or clear their artifact — call finalizeProofreadReport. An empty findings list cannot replace existing child findings. Source resolveProofreadGlossaryCandidates Accept or reject evidence-bound proper-term candidates returned by proofreading children. Accepted candidates are merged into the validated workspace glossary candidate JSON; ordinary vocabulary must be rejected. Finalization is blocked while any candidate remains pending. Source finalizeProofreadReport Validate the sole merged findings JSON artifact and close the proofreading completion gate. Call only after all split children, or after the host reports Monte Carlo convergence. Source resolveProofreadMontecarloLimit Apply the user's explicit choice after Monte Carlo reaches its round ceiling without convergence: continue for three rounds, switch only HOT regions to split review, or stop and finalize current findings. Source runProofreadSubagents Start host-planned native Pi proofreading workers in the background. In split mode, splitSize defines queued assignment blocks while workerCount only limits persistent Pi worker concurrency. The host owns every line assignment; optional worker records only select labels or configured models. Source runSubagents Delegate concrete investigation or bounded translation-repair tasks to native Pi children. Project worker settings are concurrency preferences, never an authorization gate. A translation_repair task must list every writable row in lines; fromLine/toLine are only its read-only envelope. The Host rejects unlisted writes. First locate the concrete target and evidence. Preserve each task's distinct objective; never substitute the full translation/proofreading workflow queue. Source runTranslationSubagents Start the complete native Pi translation worker queue in the background. Optional workerCount selects a concurrency ceiling within the configured project maximum; the Host still caps live workers to real assignments. The Host alone plans single-file and folder assignments from canonical split size, file order, accepted evidence, terminology priority debt, and any persisted reuse mask. Never pass tasks or ranges. Retained reuse lines are never repartitioned. Return immediately so the parent remains interactive; inspect structured cards only when needed. Source subagentRunner.ts searchProjectText Search UTF-8 files and return bounded, match-centered file/line evidence. For the canonical glossary, character bible, and glossary-candidate paths, one source/name lookup returns complete matching structured records, including their target forms and aliases; do not repeat the query against parent folders or translated spellings. A bound source document id or source filename resolves to the actual Host-bound file, including extracted EPUB text. Other relative paths use the current project; absolute paths may point to user-provided external references. Omit path, pass a blank path, or use '.' for the project root. Recursive project search excludes Pi transcripts and generated historical review HTML; pass the exact HTML path only when it is genuinely required. This tool never writes. Source repairAssignedTranslation After reading the host-reported required lines yourself with readAssignedSource, submit structured { line, translation } repairs. Never echo source text unchanged; every other translated line is already retained. Source validateAssignedTranslation Validate the assigned range and submit evidence-backed discoveries exactly once after writing. A successful call is terminal for this artifact turn. Source readAssignedProofreadContext Read the aligned source and translation for the Host-owned assignment, boundary context, deterministic host signals, and approved project references. Follow the built-in proofreading workflow in the system instructions. Source readProofreadReference Read the next bounded chunk of a project proofreading reference whose manifest entry has complete=false. Entries returned with complete=true are already fully read and must not be requested again. Start at offset 0 and continue only from the returned nextOffset. Source readBoundSourceLines Read exact one-based lines from the source document delegated by the parent. Source readBoundTranslationLines Read exact one-based lines from the current translation candidate delegated by the parent. Source readAssignedTranslationReview Read every Host-selected mechanical-risk row and deterministic clean sample with short neighboring context. Selected rows are mandatory review targets; a context row may also be rejected when it clearly shares or continues the discovered defect. Source submitTranslationReview Accept the selected review scope with no failures, or reject concrete bad lines with an actionable repair note. A clearly bad context row may be included; Host promotes it to repair debt and centers the next review window on it. Never emit per-line pass verdicts. Source readAssignedTranslationAudit Read the exact aligned source/current-translation pairs assigned for semantic reuse review. Source submitTranslationAudit Submit one semantic verdict for every assigned line that requires semantic review. Source pdfReferenceTools.ts inspectPdfReferences Read only the lightweight PDF page/figure index for source lines that mention figures, tables or other visual evidence. Specify documentId from the native manifest for a folder. No image bytes enter context. Use viewPdfReference only when that passage needs the visual; never view every page by default. TXT/EPUB documents return available=false. Source viewPdfReference View one read-only PDF image or page referenced by a source passage. First inspectPdfReferences; cite the relevant sourceLine and explain the visual ambiguity. Requires the configured model to accept images. The tool returns a native Pi image block, never an automatic attachment to every assignment. Source"},{"locale":"zh","file":"terminology.html","title":"Agent 术语","headings":[{"id":"agent","text":"Agent","level":2},{"id":"host","text":"Host","level":2},{"id":"harness","text":"Harness","level":2},{"id":"runtime","text":"Runtime","level":2},{"id":"pi","text":"Pi","level":2},{"id":"parent-agent","text":"Parent Agent","level":2},{"id":"child-agent-subagent","text":"Child Agent / Subagent","level":2},{"id":"worker","text":"Worker","level":2},{"id":"supervisor","text":"Supervisor","level":2},{"id":"provider-model","text":"Provider / Model","level":2},{"id":"prompt-system-prompt","text":"Prompt / System Prompt","level":2},{"id":"tool-function","text":"Tool / Function","level":2},{"id":"tool-call","text":"Tool Call","level":2},{"id":"workflow","text":"Workflow","level":2},{"id":"typed-contract","text":"Typed Contract","level":2},{"id":"domainrun","text":"DomainRun","level":2},{"id":"scope-ownership","text":"Scope / Ownership","level":2},{"id":"assignment","text":"Assignment","level":2},{"id":"batch","text":"Batch","level":2},{"id":"manifest","text":"Manifest","level":2},{"id":"artifact","text":"Artifact","level":2},{"id":"candidate","text":"Candidate","level":2},{"id":"canonical","text":"Canonical","level":2},{"id":"staging","text":"Staging","level":2},{"id":"promote","text":"Promote","level":2},{"id":"validator-validation","text":"Validator / Validation","level":2},{"id":"mechanical-validation","text":"Mechanical Validation","level":2},{"id":"semantic-review-reviewer","text":"Semantic Review / Reviewer","level":2},{"id":"finding-verdict","text":"Finding / Verdict","level":2},{"id":"evidence","text":"Evidence","level":2},{"id":"debt","text":"Debt","level":2},{"id":"hash-hash-bound-hash-current","text":"Hash / Hash-bound / Hash-current","level":2},{"id":"completion-gate","text":"Completion Gate","level":2},{"id":"session-jsonl","text":"Session / JSONL","level":2},{"id":"persistence-durable-state","text":"Persistence / Durable State","level":2},{"id":"atomic-transaction-rollback","text":"Atomic / Transaction / Rollback","level":2},{"id":"queue","text":"Queue","level":2},{"id":"steer-follow-up","text":"Steer / Follow-up","level":2},{"id":"context-context-window","text":"Context / Context Window","level":2},{"id":"compaction","text":"Compaction","level":2},{"id":"token-cache","text":"Token / Cache","level":2},{"id":"ipc-bridge","text":"IPC / Bridge","level":2},{"id":"main-process-renderer","text":"Main Process / Renderer","level":2},{"id":"telemetry-observability","text":"Telemetry / Observability","level":2}],"summary":"Agent 技术术语 English · 工作流 Agent 能够接收消息、调用模型、选择工具并继续推进任务的执行主体。 YN 中的 Parent 和 Child 都是 Agent，并且都运行在 Pi runtime 上。 不等于模型本身；模型只是 Agent 每一步推理时调用的能力。 Host 模型外面的可信程序层，真正执行工具、读写文件、保存状态并拒绝越权操作。 YN Host 是通用 Agent Host 里的翻译业务层，负责清单、队列、范围、校验、证据和提交。 不是远程服务器，不是主 Agent，也不是另一个模型。 Harness 把模型、消息循环、工具、状态、错误处理和完成判断连接成可运行系统的整套外壳。 本项目的 Harness 由 Pi Agent loop、YN Host、工具、Supervisor、持久化与 UI 协议共同组成。 不是一条提示词，也不是某个单独的 workflow。 Runtime Agent 实际运行时使用的代码环境与生命周期实现。 Pi runtime 负责消息、模型调用、tool call、continue、队列消息、重试和 compaction。 不是所选模型；同一个 runtime 可以切换不同 provider 和 model。 Pi 本项目采用的 Agent runtime 基础实现。 Parent 与 Child 共用 Pi 的 Agent、AgentMessage、Session 和 JSONL 语义。 不是 YN 自己另造的一套聊天协议。 Parent Agent 直接与用户对话、规划工作并汇总结果的主 Agent。 它选择阶段、调用 Host 工具、处理冲突和剩余债务，最后向用户报告。 不会代替 Host 绕过范围和校验直接写入。 Child Agent / Subagent 由 Parent 或 Host 为一项有边界任务启动的 Agent。 Child 拥有独立 Pi session，只看到当前 assignment 所需的工具和上下文。 不是一个只有函数体的后台线程，也不能再启动下一层 subagent。 Worker 反复从共享队列领取 assignment 的持久 Child 角色。 翻译 Worker 负责写 staging；审阅 Worker 只读并提交失败 verdict；校对 Worker 写 findings。 Worker 数是并发上限，不等于任务块数量。 Supervisor 管理 Child 生命周期、领取任务、重试、结算和补位的 Host 组件。 它连接 Host 队列与多个 Pi Child runtime，并保证失败 Worker 不偷偷领取下一项。 不负责生成译文内容。 Provider / Model Provider 是模型服务来源，Model 是该服务中实际调用的模型。 它们是用户级配置；Child 默认继承 Parent 当前选择。 更换模型不会更换 Host、Workflow contract 或项目资产。 Prompt / System Prompt Prompt 是交给 Agent 的本轮指令；System Prompt 是运行时注入的高优先级行为和工具说明。 页面生成的 Prompt 选择翻译或校对入口，内置 System Prompt 解释当前 typed workflow 与可用工具。 Prompt 文字本身不能授予 Host 没有给出的写权限。 Tool / Function Host 暴露给 Agent 的结构化调用接口。本文档里的 Function 指这些 tool surface。 每项都有 schema、读取边界、状态变化、返回值和拒绝条件。 不是让模型随意执行的内部 JavaScript 函数。 Tool Call Agent 请求 Host 执行某个 Tool 的结构化消息。 Host 校验参数和当前状态，执行后把 toolResult 放回同一 Pi turn。 调用成功不等于完整 workflow 已完成。 Workflow 从入口、阶段推进到完成条件的一整套工作契约。 产品只暴露 initial_translation 与 proofread 两条完整 Workflow；术语、角色、复用和 QA 是内部阶段。 不是一个方便预填 Prompt 的按钮名称。 Typed Contract 由程序结构明确记录、可以校验的约束，而不是只写在自然语言里。 文件身份、范围、worker 上限、workflow intent 和完成债务都会进入 typed state。 模型声称“我会只改这些行”不等于拥有 typed 权限。 DomainRun 一次 YN 翻译或校对 workflow 的领域状态实例。 它记录 workflow 类型、owner、inspection、batch、发现、债务和 completion 进度。 不是模型进程，也不是 UI 里的任务卡片。 Scope / Ownership Scope 是允许操作的对象与范围；Ownership 表示当前谁合法持有该范围。 文档、连续行块或精确行都由 Host 授权，读取上下文不会扩大写入 ownership。 能读到一个文件不表示能修改它。 Assignment Host 交给一个 Worker 的单个有边界工作单元。 它绑定 document、行范围或精确行、输入 hash、角色和尝试状态。 不是整个文件，也不一定与 splitSize 一一相等。 Batch 一组被同一次 Host 调度和结算管理的 assignment。 Host 在创建 Child 前原子预留 batch，并分别记录 taskCount 与实际 workerCount。 不等于一个 Child，也不等于一个文件。 Manifest 本轮工作认可的文档清单及其身份信息。 文件顺序、原文、候选路径、行数和阶段屏障都来自 authoritative manifest。 不是每次让模型重新扫描目录得到的临时列表。 Artifact 工作流产生并可被机器验证的持久文件或记录。 典型 artifact 包括行对齐候选译文、findings JSON、HTML sidecar 和项目资产。 Agent 在聊天里说“完成了”不是 artifact。 Candidate 尚处在检查、选择或确认阶段的内容。具体含义取决于对象。 translation candidate 是正式写回前的候选译文；glossary candidate 是尚未进入正式术语表的译名。 两个 candidate 的审批和存储规则并不相同。 Canonical 当前被系统视为权威、唯一结算依据的版本或位置。 可以指正式术语表、正式候选译文路径、canonical Pi messages 或唯一 findings JSON。 不表示内容永远不能再修改，只表示当前真相来源明确。 Staging 尚未提升为正式结果的可恢复待检副本。 翻译 Worker 先把负责行写入 staging；机械校验和独立审阅通过后，Host 才提升到 canonical 译文。 不是 Git staging、内存缓存或已经正式提交的译文。 Promote 把已经通过检查的 staging 范围写入 canonical artifact。 提升按精确范围并在候选文件锁内执行，不把同一 staging 的其他未审行一起带入。 不等于简单重命名整个临时文件。 Validator / Validation 用确定规则判断输入或产物是否满足契约的代码与过程。 它检查行数、占位符、标签、保留规则、范围、schema、术语和完成债务。 不等于模型阅读后觉得“看起来不错”。 Mechanical Validation 不需要模型理解语义即可重复执行的确定性检查。 例如行对齐、保护载荷、空行、明显占位文本、格式和部分术语一致性。 语义审阅检查误译、语气和上下文含义。 Semantic Review / Reviewer 结合原文、译文和上下文判断意义是否正确的审阅；Reviewer 是执行该审阅的只读 Worker。 翻译 Reviewer 只上报失败行，校对 Worker 则写入结构化 findings。 Reviewer 不直接修改翻译 staging。 Finding / Verdict Finding 是校对中可交付的问题记录；Verdict 是对某项检查的结构化结论。 findings 进入唯一 JSON 和审阅 HTML；review verdict 通常只记录失败或 reuse/retranslate。 不是聊天中的自由散文评论。 Evidence 支持一个结论、并能在恢复后重新核对的结构化依据。 证据会绑定文档、行、代码、参考资产及 source/candidate hash。 只写一句理由但无法定位原译文，不算充分证据。 Debt 工作流在允许完成前仍必须处理的明确事项。 可能是未翻译行、术语修复、warning 真阳性、未覆盖 scope 或待决资产。 不是技术债务的泛称，而是 completion gate 可计算的未结项。 Hash / Hash-bound / Hash-current Hash 是内容指纹；hash-bound 表示结论绑定某份具体输入；hash-current 表示指纹仍与当前文件一致。 输入变化时只让相关证据和授权失效，避免把旧结论套到新文本。 相同 Hash 用于识别未变化的内容。 Completion Gate 决定 workflow 是否真的满足完成条件的程序门槛。 它核对 assignment 结算、coverage、验证、术语和资产债务，而不是相信模型的完成声明。 Agent 发出最终回复不代表 completion gate 已通过。 Session / JSONL Session 是一条可继续的 Agent 会话；JSONL 是按行追加保存会话事件的文件格式。 Parent 与每个 Child 都有自己的 Pi JSONL，用于恢复、审计和按需展开。 Parent 卡片里不会复制完整 Child transcript。 Persistence / Durable State 把关键状态写到磁盘，使进程关闭后仍能恢复。Durable 表示不是只存在内存里。 Pi messages、Host state、staging、审阅证据和复用审计都有持久边界。 控制台日志不是唯一持久证据。 Atomic / Transaction / Rollback Atomic 表示相关变更要么全部成功，要么不留下半套结果；Transaction 是这组提交边界；Rollback 是失败后恢复旧状态。 术语状态、staging 提升、canonical 文件与 Host evidence 都使用明确事务边界。 不是先写一部分，失败后靠下次运行猜测修补。 Queue 等待 Worker 领取的 assignment 集合。 共享队列按文件阶段开放；术语 priority wave 未结算时，普通任务不能越过它。 不是给每个 Worker 预先分一整份私有文件列表。 Steer / Follow-up Steer 是希望当前工具结束后尽快让同一 Agent 看到的补充；Follow-up 是排在当前工作之后的消息。 两者都保留原始 AgentMessage，并由同一 Pi harness 消费。 不是另建一套 YN 消息队列或等待状态机。 Context / Context Window 模型在一次调用中实际看到的消息和资料；Context Window 是模型能容纳的 Token 容量。 Host 只注入负责行、短边界、命中资产和当前债务，完整状态留在磁盘。 项目里存在一个文件不表示它已被塞进模型上下文。 Compaction 长会话接近上下文容量时，把较早内容压缩为可继续使用的摘要。 使用 Pi 0.99.1 原生 compaction entry、retainedTail 与 branch 上下文投影，不另造 YN 摘要文件。 不是删除完整 JSONL；原始历史仍可审计。 Token / Cache Token 是模型处理文本的计量单位；Cache 是服务商或运行时对重复输入的复用。 节省 Token 主要依靠有界上下文、直接命中资产、持久 Worker 和只上报失败行。 不能靠一个魔法 Token 上限强行阻断合法调查。 IPC / Bridge IPC 是进程间通信；Bridge 是把受限能力安全暴露给页面的接口层。 Renderer 通过 Electron bridge 请求 main process 保存项目、读资产、启动 Agent 或写入文件。 网页脚本不能因此直接获得任意磁盘权限。 Main Process / Renderer Main Process 是 Electron 中持有系统能力的后端进程；Renderer 是显示 React 或 HTML 界面的前端进程。 Agent runtime、文件和 Host 状态属于 main；页面负责输入与结构化展示。 Renderer 显示的状态不能取代 main 中的持久真相。 Telemetry / Observability Telemetry 是运行指标与事件；Observability 是利用这些证据判断系统内部发生了什么的能力。 关键证据包括 provider 错误链、assignment、staging、review debt、队列状态和 completion 原因。 不是在界面上堆满内部 ID 和裸协议文本。"},{"locale":"en","file":"terminology.en.html","title":"Agent terminology","headings":[{"id":"agent","text":"Agent","level":2},{"id":"host","text":"Host","level":2},{"id":"harness","text":"Harness","level":2},{"id":"runtime","text":"Runtime","level":2},{"id":"pi","text":"Pi","level":2},{"id":"parent-agent","text":"Parent Agent","level":2},{"id":"child-agent-subagent","text":"Child Agent / Subagent","level":2},{"id":"worker","text":"Worker","level":2},{"id":"supervisor","text":"Supervisor","level":2},{"id":"provider-model","text":"Provider / Model","level":2},{"id":"prompt-system-prompt","text":"Prompt / System Prompt","level":2},{"id":"tool-function","text":"Tool / Function","level":2},{"id":"tool-call","text":"Tool Call","level":2},{"id":"workflow","text":"Workflow","level":2},{"id":"typed-contract","text":"Typed Contract","level":2},{"id":"domainrun","text":"DomainRun","level":2},{"id":"scope-ownership","text":"Scope / Ownership","level":2},{"id":"assignment","text":"Assignment","level":2},{"id":"batch","text":"Batch","level":2},{"id":"manifest","text":"Manifest","level":2},{"id":"artifact","text":"Artifact","level":2},{"id":"candidate","text":"Candidate","level":2},{"id":"canonical","text":"Canonical","level":2},{"id":"staging","text":"Staging","level":2},{"id":"promote","text":"Promote","level":2},{"id":"validator-validation","text":"Validator / Validation","level":2},{"id":"mechanical-validation","text":"Mechanical Validation","level":2},{"id":"semantic-review-reviewer","text":"Semantic Review / Reviewer","level":2},{"id":"finding-verdict","text":"Finding / Verdict","level":2},{"id":"evidence","text":"Evidence","level":2},{"id":"debt","text":"Debt","level":2},{"id":"hash-hash-bound-hash-current","text":"Hash / Hash-bound / Hash-current","level":2},{"id":"completion-gate","text":"Completion Gate","level":2},{"id":"session-jsonl","text":"Session / JSONL","level":2},{"id":"persistence-durable-state","text":"Persistence / Durable State","level":2},{"id":"atomic-transaction-rollback","text":"Atomic / Transaction / Rollback","level":2},{"id":"queue","text":"Queue","level":2},{"id":"steer-follow-up","text":"Steer / Follow-up","level":2},{"id":"context-context-window","text":"Context / Context Window","level":2},{"id":"compaction","text":"Compaction","level":2},{"id":"token-cache","text":"Token / Cache","level":2},{"id":"ipc-bridge","text":"IPC / Bridge","level":2},{"id":"main-process-renderer","text":"Main Process / Renderer","level":2},{"id":"telemetry-observability","text":"Telemetry / Observability","level":2}],"summary":"Agent terminology 中文 · Workflows Agent An execution unit that receives messages, invokes a model, selects tools, and keeps a task moving. Both Parent and Child are Agents running on the Pi runtime. It is not the model itself; the model is one capability used during an Agent turn. Host The trusted program layer outside the model that executes tools, reads and writes files, persists state, and rejects invalid operations. The YN Host is the translation-domain part of the broader Agent host. It owns manifests, queues, scopes, validation, evidence, and commits. It is not a remote server, the Parent Agent, or another model. Harness The surrounding system that connects models, message loops, tools, state, error handling, and completion checks into a working agent. Here it includes the Pi Agent loop, YN Host, tools, Supervisor, persistence, and UI protocol. It is not a single prompt or one workflow. Runtime The code environment and lifecycle implementation in which an Agent actually runs. The Pi runtime handles messages, model calls, tool calls, continue, queued messages, retries, and compaction. It is not the selected model; one runtime can use different providers and models. Pi The base Agent runtime used by this project. Parent and Child share Pi Agent, AgentMessage, Session, and JSONL semantics. It is not a separate chat protocol invented by YN. Parent Agent The primary Agent that talks to the user, plans the work, and consolidates results. It advances stages, calls Host tools, resolves conflicts and remaining debt, and reports the outcome. It cannot bypass Host scope and validation rules. Child Agent / Subagent An Agent started by the Parent or Host for a bounded task. A Child has its own Pi session and sees only the tools and context required by its current assignment. It is not merely a background thread and cannot spawn another subagent layer. Worker A persistent Child role that repeatedly claims assignments from a shared queue. Translation Workers write staging, review Workers submit only failed verdicts, and proofread Workers write findings. Worker count is a concurrency limit, not the number of task chunks. Supervisor The Host component that manages Child lifecycles, task claims, retries, settlement, and replacement workers. It connects the Host queue to Pi Child runtimes and prevents a failed Worker from silently claiming more work. It does not generate translation content. Provider / Model A Provider supplies model access; a Model is the specific model invoked through that service. They are user-level settings, and Children inherit the Parent selection by default. Changing the model does not replace the Host, workflow contract, or project assets. Prompt / System Prompt A Prompt is the instruction for a turn; a System Prompt is higher-priority runtime guidance about behavior and tools. The page prompt selects translation or proofreading, while the built-in System Prompt explains the active typed workflow and tools. Prompt wording cannot grant write authority that the Host did not provide. Tool / Function A structured call interface exposed by the Host to an Agent. This manual uses Function for these tool surfaces. Each surface has a schema, read boundary, state transition, result, and rejection conditions. It is not an arbitrary internal JavaScript function available to the model. Tool Call A structured message in which an Agent asks the Host to execute a Tool. The Host validates arguments and current state, executes the operation, and returns a toolResult to the same Pi turn. A successful call does not mean the whole workflow is complete. Workflow A complete work contract from entry point through staged execution to completion conditions. The product exposes only initial_translation and proofread as full workflows; terminology, character handling, reuse, and QA are internal stages. It is not merely a button that prefills a prompt. Typed Contract A machine-structured, enforceable constraint rather than a promise written only in natural language. Document identity, scope, worker limit, workflow intent, and completion debt are stored as typed state. A model saying it will edit only certain lines is not typed authorization. DomainRun The domain-state instance for one YN translation or proofreading workflow. It records workflow kind, owner, inspection, batches, discoveries, debt, and completion progress. It is not a model process or a UI task card. Scope / Ownership Scope defines what may be operated on; Ownership identifies who currently holds legal authority over that scope. Documents, contiguous ranges, and exact lines are Host-authorized, and reading context never expands write ownership. Being able to read a file does not imply permission to modify it. Assignment One bounded unit of work assigned by the Host to a Worker. It binds a document, range or exact lines, input hash, worker role, and attempt state. It is not necessarily a whole file or always equal to splitSize. Batch A set of assignments managed and settled by one Host scheduling operation. The Host atomically reserves the batch before creating Children and records taskCount separately from workerCount. It is not one Child or one file. Manifest The authoritative document list and identities for the current run. File order, source and candidate paths, line counts, and stage barriers come from this manifest. It is not a temporary directory listing reconstructed by the model every turn. Artifact A durable file or record produced by a workflow and subject to machine validation. Typical artifacts include aligned translation candidates, findings JSON, HTML sidecars, and project assets. An Agent saying 'done' in chat is not an artifact. Candidate Content still awaiting inspection, selection, or confirmation; its exact meaning depends on the object. A translation candidate is output awaiting final write-back, while a glossary candidate is a term not yet in the approved glossary. The two candidate types do not share the same approval or storage rules. Canonical The version or location currently treated as authoritative for settlement. It may describe the approved glossary, canonical translation path, canonical Pi messages, or the single findings JSON. It does not mean immutable forever; it means the current source of truth is unambiguous. Staging A recoverable, inspectable copy that has not yet been promoted to the official result. Translation Workers write their lines to staging first; the Host promotes them only after mechanical validation and independent review. It is not Git staging, an in-memory cache, or already committed translation output. Promote To write an accepted staging range into the canonical artifact. Promotion is range-scoped and candidate-locked, so unrelated unreviewed staging lines are not included. It is not simply renaming an entire temporary file. Validator / Validation Code and process that use deterministic rules to decide whether input or output satisfies a contract. It checks line counts, placeholders, tags, preserve rules, scope, schema, terminology, and completion debt. It is not a model saying the result looks good. Mechanical Validation Deterministic checks that can be repeated without asking a model to understand meaning. Examples include alignment, protected payloads, blank lines, obvious placeholder text, formatting, and some terminology consistency. Semantic review examines meaning, tone and context. Semantic Review / Reviewer Review that uses source, translation, and context to judge meaning; a Reviewer is the read-only Worker performing it. Translation Reviewers report only failed lines, while proofread Workers write structured findings. A Reviewer does not directly edit translation staging. Finding / Verdict A Finding is a deliverable proofreading issue; a Verdict is a structured decision for a check. Findings enter the single JSON and review HTML, while review verdicts usually record only failures or reuse/retranslate. They are not free-form chat commentary. Evidence Structured support for a conclusion that can be checked again after recovery. Evidence is bound to document, line, code, reference asset, and source/candidate hashes. A vague reason that cannot be traced to source and translation is insufficient. Debt A concrete item that must be settled before the workflow may complete. It may be untranslated lines, terminology repair, true-positive warnings, uncovered scopes, or pending assets. Here it is not a vague synonym for technical debt; it is computable unfinished work. Hash / Hash-bound / Hash-current A hash is a content fingerprint; hash-bound means a conclusion is tied to specific input, and hash-current means it still matches the current files. When input changes, only the relevant evidence and authority are invalidated instead of applying stale conclusions to new text. Matching hashes identify unchanged content. Completion Gate The programmatic gate that decides whether a workflow has actually satisfied its completion contract. It checks assignment settlement, coverage, validation, terminology, and asset debt instead of trusting a model's completion claim. An Agent final response does not mean the gate has passed. Session / JSONL A Session is a continuable Agent conversation; JSONL stores its events as append-only JSON lines. The Parent and every Child have separate Pi JSONL files for recovery, audit, and on-demand expansion. The Parent card does not embed the full Child transcript. Persistence / Durable State Writing critical state to disk so it survives process shutdown; durable means it is not memory-only. Pi messages, Host state, staging, review evidence, and reuse audits all have persistence boundaries. Console logs are not the sole durable evidence. Atomic / Transaction / Rollback Atomic means related changes all succeed or leave no partial result; a Transaction is that commit boundary, and Rollback restores prior state after failure. Terminology state, staging promotion, canonical files, and Host evidence use explicit transaction boundaries. It is not partial writing followed by a later run guessing how to repair it. Queue The set of assignments waiting to be claimed by Workers. The shared queue opens by file stage, and ordinary work cannot pass an unsettled terminology priority wave. It is not a private whole-file list assigned to each Worker in advance. Steer / Follow-up A Steer is an update for the same Agent to consume soon after the current tool returns; a Follow-up waits until the current work finishes. Both remain original AgentMessage objects and are consumed by the same Pi harness. They do not create a separate YN message queue or waiting state machine. Context / Context Window The messages and references visible to a model call; the Context Window is the model's token capacity. The Host injects owned lines, short boundaries, direct asset matches, and current debt while keeping full state on disk. A file existing in the project does not mean it was loaded into model context. Compaction Compressing older conversation content into a usable summary when a long session approaches context limits. YN uses Pi 0.99.1 native compaction entries, retainedTail and branch context projection rather than a separate summary file. It does not delete the full JSONL history. Token / Cache A Token is a unit of model text processing; Cache reuses repeated input at the provider or runtime layer. YN saves tokens through bounded context, direct asset matches, persistent Workers, and failure-only review output. A magic token cap must not block legitimate investigation. IPC / Bridge IPC is inter-process communication; a Bridge exposes a controlled capability surface to a page. The Renderer asks the Electron main process to save projects, read assets, start Agents, or write files through the bridge. This does not give page scripts unrestricted disk access. Main Process / Renderer The Electron Main Process owns system capabilities; a Renderer displays the React or HTML interface. Agent runtime, files, and Host state live in main, while pages collect input and render structured output. Renderer state cannot replace durable truth in main. Telemetry / Observability Telemetry is runtime metrics and events; Observability is the ability to infer internal behavior from that evidence. Key evidence includes provider error chains, assignments, staging, review debt, queue state, and completion reasons. It does not mean flooding the UI with internal IDs and raw protocol text."},{"locale":"zh","file":"changelog.html","title":"版本记录","headings":[{"id":"2-2-4-更新","text":"2.2.4 更新","level":2},{"id":"2-2-3-更新","text":"2.2.3 更新","level":2},{"id":"2-2-2-更新","text":"2.2.2 更新","level":2},{"id":"2-2-1-更新","text":"2.2.1 更新","level":2},{"id":"2-2-0-更新","text":"2.2.0 更新","level":2},{"id":"2-1-9-更新","text":"2.1.9 更新","level":2},{"id":"2-1-7-2-1-8-更新","text":"2.1.7–2.1.8 更新","level":2},{"id":"2-1-6-更新","text":"2.1.6 更新","level":2},{"id":"2-1-5-更新","text":"2.1.5 更新","level":2},{"id":"2-1-4-更新","text":"2.1.4 更新","level":2},{"id":"2-1-3-更新","text":"2.1.3 更新","level":2},{"id":"2-1-2-更新","text":"2.1.2 更新","level":2},{"id":"2-0-5-2-1-0-更新","text":"2.0.5 → 2.1.0 更新","level":2},{"id":"2-0-1-2-0-5-工作流可靠性与-provider","text":"2.0.1 – 2.0.5：工作流可靠性与 Provider","level":3}],"summary":"更新记录 English · 项目首页 以下保留已记录的版本变化；公开发行与下载以 Releases 为准。 2.2.4 更新 校对应用前自动载入完整译文并保留人工修改，避免 EPUB 等单文件导出出现空行。 翻译结束的可选警告审查提供“继续／跳过”选择，继续后自动续跑。 2.2.3 更新 文件夹校对应用后自动刷新审阅页面，保留人工修改和当前子文件。 修复 Agent 对齐检查的状态反馈，正确显示并读取未通过项。 2.2.2 更新 修复校对跳转未复用已导入译文的 HTML，以及重建页面缺少 EPUB 导出的问题。 2.2.1 更新 优化项目路径解析，保持校对应用、正文跳转和导出绑定一致，支持项目移动后继续使用。 2.2.0 更新 新增文字层 PDF 翻译：提取正文及公式、代码、图表等资产，整理并审计文档结构后生成审阅 HTML，再用译文和保留资产自动重排生成新 PDF。支持完整段落、跨页续段和段内公式调序，保留代码、公式及参考文献。详见 PDF 使用说明。 新增官方后台 Agent API，复用项目准备、翻译、校对和资料整理流程，支持状态查询、停止、续跑和用户答复。 改善大项目处理：大历史会话和候选译文在后台加载、校验与导入，支持进度和取消；优化会话恢复及分块缓存复用。 改善编辑体验：生成后自动进入 HTML，优化已有页面打开、译文导入、保存和关窗流程，保留人工修改。 减少英文标识和角色名触发的漏译、术语误报，支持主 Agent 对具体漏译误报进行确认。 2.1.9 更新 修复 2.1.4 带来的单文件模式回归。 2.1.7–2.1.8 更新 漏译检查排除正则实际匹配的保留内容，以及术语表中在同一行正确对应的源词与译词；其余正文仍需翻译。用户明确要求保留的词由 Agent 记录为正式的「源词 → 原词」，候选导入和 AI 审阅使用相同规则。译名匹配、术语冲突及恢复重扫也排除正则保留片段。 审阅绑定失效后，由 Host 停止旧工人、核验草稿并自动续跑；保留未变化行的通过证据，修复停止时的批次结算错误。 2.1.6 更新 已绑定的必需文件缺失时停止整个工作流，保留草稿并提示恢复路径；未绑定的译名表、角色表允许缺省。 修复立即中止与项目关闭的收尾死锁。 修复 Electron HTML 关闭与停止任务的路径绑定；保存失败会明确提示并保留修改。 项目内设置、HTML 和恢复产物使用相对路径；复制整个项目后仍可读取父/子 Agent 历史、草稿和审阅记录。项目外绑定的原文或资料需一并带走并重新选择。 2.1.5 更新 修复大文件翻译卡死：分块检查只扫描当前范围，全文终检在后台执行，保留全部结构要求、审阅与中断恢复。 校对建议复用翻译的格式保留要求与机械检查，防止丢失控制符、标签和占位符。 修复并发中断恢复：Host 在启动 Worker 前统一核查、交接已有译文、staging 与审阅记录；提交失败保留可恢复产物，不可重试的内部错误停止整个工作流。 2.1.4 更新 整理参考资料可直接新建并绑定项目，在翻译前准备译名表和角色表；首页支持一键清空填写内容并恢复默认参数。 资料整理先生成可修改、删除的草稿，核查后一次性提交正式译名表和角色表；中断或失败保留草稿。 简便启动先核对参数与原文、试跑控制符保留规则，再使用 HTML 共用参数表和相同翻译提示词；需要人工介入时可先生成行对行 HTML。 移除无效的分块开关，保留每块行数；文件夹 HTML 自动填入带大括号的文件顺序，保留已填写的选择。 首页顶部可直接配置供应商和模型，无需先选择项目或打开 HTML；设置全局共用。 首页新增内置 Agent 任务入口：确认参数后自动打开 HTML 并启动翻译或校对，也可直接整理项目资料。默认分块 500 行、子 Agent 上限 3；翻译前预扫并试跑保留规则。 HTML 新增角色表查看、编辑和删除；校对可自动应用意见到 HTML，TXT 仍手动保存。 修复停止后旧任务或压缩仍继续启动的竞态。 2.1.3 更新 修复 Grok 4.7 被误发 reasoning_effort=none 的请求：自动及旧“关闭”配置使用官方默认 high，没有已知思考档位的模型不发送 effort 参数。 HTML 术语面板分别显示正式译名表与 AI 候选，导入前可查看、搜索和删除候选，正式表也支持逐条删除。删除仅修改对应表，不自动修改译文或角色资料；旧 HTML 打开时会自动升级。 内核升级到 0.99.1，并完成各方面适配，避免回归。 2.1.2 更新 标准 Provider 的模型目录可从 Pi 上游自动刷新，并在网络不可用时使用本地缓存或随应用发布的目录。 修复停放的译文复用流程恢复、校对术语候选重试和 Workflow 类型恢复中的状态不一致。 500 行模型分页与结构化修复上限保持一致，并合并同一行重复的长度风险信号。 2.0.5 → 2.1.0 更新 超大审阅页能打开了：不再被 80 MiB 卡死；建议跳到原文，实测从大约 4 秒降到 1–2 秒。 大文件翻译、校对更稳，内存不再越跑越高，预扫描也不再卡住主窗口。 主窗口能自适应；角色可以给同一人追加多条台词。 打开 Agent 或发短问题，不会把审阅页拉回顶部。 手机远程改成全屏工作区，Agent 放进工具抽屉。 2.0.1 – 2.0.5：工作流可靠性与 Provider 校对与 EPUB 始终遵循页面手选的权威译文绑定；翻译完成后，未手选的页面会跟随正式 translated 产物，不再误读临时快照。 新增 Grok (OAuth)、按模型适配的思考等级和长推理等待；授权过期时刷新并恢复当前工作，而不是中断整批任务。 翻译复审耗尽后把精确失败行交回主 Agent，校对 findings 由 Host 按当前绑定行校正；已通过结果不会被后续空写入或失败项清空。 术语长名覆盖短名，跨文件术语差异进入最终警告复核；关闭术语候选时不再构造、更新或校验候选资产。 批量应用保留人工修改和 TXT 写入状态，恢复命令明确区分翻译与校对，减少跨工作流误恢复。"},{"locale":"en","file":"changelog.en.html","title":"Changelog","headings":[{"id":"what-s-new-in-2-2-4","text":"What's new in 2.2.4","level":2},{"id":"what-s-new-in-2-2-3","text":"What's new in 2.2.3","level":2},{"id":"what-s-new-in-2-2-2","text":"What's new in 2.2.2","level":2},{"id":"what-s-new-in-2-2-1","text":"What's new in 2.2.1","level":2},{"id":"what-s-new-in-2-2-0","text":"What's new in 2.2.0","level":2},{"id":"what-s-new-in-2-1-9","text":"What's new in 2.1.9","level":2},{"id":"what-s-new-in-2-1-7-2-1-8","text":"What's new in 2.1.7–2.1.8","level":2},{"id":"what-s-new-in-2-1-6","text":"What's new in 2.1.6","level":2},{"id":"what-s-new-in-2-1-5","text":"What's new in 2.1.5","level":2},{"id":"what-s-new-in-2-1-4","text":"What's new in 2.1.4","level":2},{"id":"what-s-new-in-2-1-3","text":"What's new in 2.1.3","level":2},{"id":"what-s-new-in-2-1-2","text":"What's new in 2.1.2","level":2},{"id":"what-s-new-from-2-0-5-to-2-1-0","text":"What's new from 2.0.5 to 2.1.0","level":2},{"id":"2-0-1-2-0-5-workflow-reliability-and-providers","text":"2.0.1 – 2.0.5: Workflow reliability and Providers","level":3}],"summary":"Changelog 中文 · Project Recorded version changes. Public availability and downloads follow Releases. What's new in 2.2.4 Load the complete translation before applying proofreading, preserving manual edits and preventing blank lines in EPUB and other single-file exports. Offer an explicit review/skip choice for optional translation warnings and continue automatically after review is selected. What's new in 2.2.3 Keep folder review pages usable after applying proofreading, preserving manual edits and the selected file. Show unresolved alignment failures and keep repair reads bound to the correct document. What's new in 2.2.2 Fix proofreading navigation to reuse imported translations in the original HTML and preserve EPUB export when rebuilding a missing page. What's new in 2.2.1 Improved project path resolution keeps proofreading changes, navigation and exports bound to the same document, including after moving a project. What's new in 2.2.0 Add text-layer PDF translation: extract prose, formulas, code and figure assets, organize and audit the document structure, then generate review HTML and reflow translated prose with preserved assets into a new PDF. Support complete paragraphs, page continuations and paragraph-local formula reordering while preserving code, formulas and references. See the PDF guide. Add the official background Agent API, reusing project preparation, translation, proofreading and reference workflows, with status queries, Stop, resume and user replies. Improve large-project handling: load large histories and validate/import translation candidates in the background with progress and cancellation; optimize session recovery and cross-chunk cache reuse. Improve editing: activate generated HTML automatically and streamline page opening, translation imports, saving and closing while preserving manual edits. Reduce false untranslated and terminology findings from English identifiers and character names; let the parent Agent confirm specific untranslated false positives. What's new in 2.1.9 Fix the single-file mode regression introduced in 2.1.4. What's new in 2.1.7–2.1.8 Exclude actual regex-preserved matches and correctly aligned glossary pairs from untranslated checks. Record explicitly preserved words as formal source-to-identical-target terms; validate the remaining prose with the same rules for candidate imports and AI review. Glossary matching, terminology conflicts, and recovery rescans also exclude regex-preserved spans. Automatically reconcile stale review bindings in Host, retain unchanged accepted evidence, and resume work. Fix batch settlement after Stop. What's new in 2.1.6 Stop when bound required files disappear, preserving drafts and reporting the missing path. Unbound glossary and character tables remain optional. Fix Stop and project shutdown deadlocks. Fix Electron HTML closing and task cancellation bindings; failed saves report the error and preserve edits. Use relative bindings for project settings, HTML and recovery artifacts. Copying a complete project retains parent/child Agent history, drafts and review evidence. External source/reference files must be transferred and selected again. What's new in 2.1.5 Fix large-file translation freezes with range-scoped chunk checks and background final validation, preserving structural checks, review and recovery. Apply translation preservation rules and mechanical checks to proofreading suggestions to protect control codes, tags and placeholders. Fix concurrent recovery: Host verifies and reconciles translations, staging and review evidence before starting Workers. Failed commits preserve recoverable artifacts; unretryable internal errors stop the workflow. What's new in 2.1.4 Create a project from reference preparation before translating. Clear homepage entries and restore task defaults in one click. Reference preparation uses editable drafts, checks them, then commits both formal assets together. Interrupted or failed tasks retain their drafts. One-click setup checks parameters against the source and trials control-token rules, then uses the shared HTML parameters and translation prompt. Generate line-by-line HTML first for hands-on control. Removed the unused chunking toggle. Folder HTML initializes the file order inside braces and preserves explicit selections. Configure providers and models at the top of the homepage before opening a project or HTML; settings are shared globally. Built-in task setup opens HTML and starts translation or proofreading after settings confirmation; reference materials can be organized directly. Defaults: 500 lines and up to 3 agents, with preservation-rule scanning before translation. Editable HTML character tables and optional proofreading auto-apply to HTML; TXT saving remains manual. Fixed canceled tasks and compaction starting after Stop. What's new in 2.1.3 Fixed Grok 4.7 requests incorrectly sending reasoning_effort=none: Auto and legacy Off selections use the official high default; models without known effort controls omit the parameter. HTML glossary management separates approved terms and AI candidates. Preview, search and delete candidates before import, or delete approved entries individually. Deletion affects only the selected table; older HTML upgrades when opened. Upgrade the core to 0.99.1 with compatibility updates to prevent regressions. What's new in 2.1.2 Standard Provider model catalogs can refresh automatically from upstream Pi, with local cache and bundled-catalog fallback when the network is unavailable. Fixed inconsistent state when resuming parked translation-reuse workflows, retrying proofreading glossary candidates, and restoring typed Workflow intent. Aligned structured repair capacity with the 500-line model page and merged duplicate length-risk signals for the same line. What's new from 2.0.5 to 2.1.0 Very large review pages open now: the 80 MiB hard reject is gone, and jumping from a suggestion to the source dropped from about 4s to 1–2s in testing. Large-file translation and proofreading are steadier: memory no longer climbs without bound, and prescans no longer freeze the main window. The main window is responsive, and a character can have multiple dialogue lines. Opening Agent or sending a short prompt no longer yanks the review page to the top. Mobile remote is a full-screen workspace, with Agent in the tools drawer. 2.0.1 – 2.0.5: Workflow reliability and Providers Proofreading and EPUB jobs consistently follow the translation explicitly selected on the page. When no file was selected manually, completed translation output becomes the authoritative translated binding instead of a temporary snapshot. Added Grok (OAuth), model-specific thinking levels, and long-reasoning waits. Expired authorization refreshes and resumes the current work instead of stopping the entire batch. Exhausted translation review hands exact failed lines back to the parent Agent. The Host refreshes proofreading findings from current bound rows, and accepted results cannot be erased by a later empty write or rejected item. Longer glossary names cover shorter names, cross-file terminology differences move to final warning review, and disabling glossary candidates also disables their construction, updates, and validation. Batch apply preserves human edits and TXT-written status. Workflow recovery explicitly distinguishes translation from proofreading to avoid resuming the wrong job."}]};
